	"quest-stone-flint-desc": "Tool heads are knapped from hard stone. Only some stones can be knapped.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Pick up three loose stones that can be knapped: flint, chert, obsidian, granite, andesite, basalt or peridotite. They lie on the ground and can be mixed kinds.<br><br><strong>Tip:</strong> Soft stones such as chalk, limestone and sandstone cannot be knapped.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-starterguide\">starter guide</a> and the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-progressionguide\">progression guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-stone-forage": "Forage for Some Food",
	"quest-stone-forage-desc": "Before you can hunt or farm, you eat what the land gives.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Pick berries from bushes, pull cattail roots at the water's edge, or gather mushrooms. Have any food item on you.<br><br><strong>Tip:</strong> Some mushrooms are poisonous. Check the handbook before you eat one.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-starterguide\">starter guide</a> and the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-progressionguide\">progression guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-stone-sticks": "Gather Sticks",
	"quest-stone-sticks-desc": "Sticks are tool handles, fire fuel and building material.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Pick up loose sticks from the forest floor, or break leafy branches to shake some out. Carry eight.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-starterguide\">starter guide</a> and the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-progressionguide\">progression guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-stone-ground": "Ground Storage",
	"quest-stone-ground-desc": "You can lay things on the ground long before you own a chest.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Sneak and right-click the ground with a stack of sticks, stones or firewood to set it down as a pile.<br><br><strong>Tip:</strong> Piles do not despawn, so this is safe storage near your camp.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://gamemechanicinfo-groundstorage\">ground storage guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-stone-spearh": "Knap a Spear Head",
	"quest-stone-spearh-desc": "A spear lets you hunt from a distance.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Sneak and right-click the ground with flint to start knapping, pick the spear head, then strike away the orange parts with a second stone.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-knapping\">knapping guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-stone-spear": "Craft Spear",
	"quest-stone-spear-desc": "A finished spear can be thrown or used in the hand.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Put the spear head and a stick together in the crafting grid.<br><br><strong>Tip:</strong> Pick your spear back up after a throw. It loses a little durability each time.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-starterguide\">starter guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-stone-hunt": "Go Hunting",
	"quest-stone-hunt-desc": "Meat, hides, fat and bones all come from animals.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Hunt any animal. Hares and chickens are easy; a boar or a ram fights back. The game counts the kill for you.<br><br><strong>Tip:</strong> Stay away from wolves and bears until you have armour.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-starterguide\">starter guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-stone-skin": "Skin and Butcher",
	"quest-stone-skin-desc": "A dead animal has to be butchered before it gives anything.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Hold a knife, look at the animal and hold the right mouse button until it opens. Take the meat, hide and fat.<br><br><strong>Tip:</strong> Do it soon. The carcass rots.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-starterguide\">starter guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-stone-catch-0": "Have any cooked meat",
	"quest-stone-catch": "Cook Your Catch",
	"quest-stone-catch-desc": "Raw meat is poor food. Cooked meat is a real meal.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Place the raw meat in a lit fire pit and wait until it is cooked. Carry one piece of cooked meat.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-starterguide\">starter guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-stone-axeh": "Knap an Axe Head",
	"quest-stone-axeh-desc": "An axe is how you get wood in any real amount.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Knap an axe head from flint the same way you made the spear head.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-knapping\">knapping guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-stone-axe": "Craft Axe",
	"quest-stone-axe-desc": "With an axe you can fell whole trees.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Put the axe head and a stick together in the crafting grid.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-starterguide\">starter guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-stone-chop": "Chop Wood",
	"quest-stone-chop-desc": "Logs are fuel and your first building material.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Find a tree and chop the lowest log with the axe. The whole tree comes down. Pick up a log.<br><br><strong>Tip:</strong> Bigger trees take longer but give far more wood.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-starterguide\">starter guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-stone-fw": "Firewood",
	"quest-stone-fw-desc": "Firewood burns longer than sticks and stacks neatly.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Put an axe and a log in the crafting grid to split it into firewood. Carry eight.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-starterguide\">starter guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-stone-knifeh": "Knap a Knife Blade",
	"quest-stone-knifeh-desc": "A knife cuts grass and reeds and butchers animals.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Knap a knife blade from flint.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-knapping\">knapping guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-stone-knife": "Craft Knife",
	"quest-stone-knife-desc": "The knife is the tool you will use most in the first days.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Put the knife blade and a stick together in the crafting grid.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-starterguide\">starter guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-stone-grass": "Cut Grass",
	"quest-stone-grass-desc": "Dry grass is tinder, bedding and thatch.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Cut tall grass with the knife and pick up the dry grass that drops. Carry eight.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-starterguide\">starter guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-stone-cat": "Cut Cattails",
	"quest-stone-cat-desc": "Cattails and papyrus are woven into baskets, mats and roofs.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Cut cattails at the edge of ponds and rivers with the knife. Carry eight tops.<br><br><strong>Tip:</strong> Leave the roots in and the plant grows back.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-starterguide\">starter guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-stone-starter": "Make a Fire Starter",
	"quest-stone-starter-desc": "A fire starter lights fires without a torch.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Craft one from a stick and dry grass in the crafting grid.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-starterguide\">starter guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-stone-fire": "Make a Fire",
	"quest-stone-fire-desc": "A fire pit cooks food, gives light and keeps you warm at night.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Sneak and right-click the ground with dry grass, add firewood the same way, then hold the fire starter on it until it catches.<br><br><strong>Tip:</strong> Keep fire away from grass and wooden walls.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-starterguide\">starter guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-stone-torch": "Make Torches",
	"quest-stone-torch-desc": "Torches let you see at night and in caves.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Put a stick in a lit fire pit to make a torch.<br><br><strong>Tip:</strong> A torch in your off hand lights your way while you work.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-starterguide\">starter guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-stone-bed": "Construct a Hay Bed",
	"quest-stone-bed-desc": "A bed lets you sleep through the night.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Craft a hay bed from dry grass and place it somewhere dry and enclosed. Set it down in the world to finish the quest.<br><br><strong>Tip:</strong> Sleeping only works when it is dark and you are not hungry.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-starterguide\">starter guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-stone-basket": "Weave Baskets",
	"quest-stone-basket-desc": "A reed basket is your first container.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Weave one from cattail tops or papyrus in the crafting grid and place it on the ground.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-starterguide\">starter guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-stone-chest": "Primitive Chests",
	"quest-stone-chest-desc": "A reed chest is storage you can make long before you have boards and nails.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Weave a reed chest from cattails or papyrus in the crafting grid. Set it down in the world to finish the quest.<br><br><strong>Tip:</strong> A wooden chest holds more, but it needs a saw, and that means copper.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-starterguide\">starter guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-stone-rope": "Make Rope",
	"quest-stone-rope-desc": "Rope is needed for ladders, traps and many later tools.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Twist dry grass or cattails together in the crafting grid.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-starterguide\">starter guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-stone-heal": "Primitive Healing",
	"quest-stone-heal-desc": "A poultice heals wounds that food and rest will not.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Wrap horsetail in reeds or linen to make a poultice. Hold the right mouse button to use it.<br><br><strong>Tip:</strong> Horsetail grows near water.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-starterguide\">starter guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-stone-shovh": "Knap a Shovel Head",
	"quest-stone-shovh-desc": "A shovel digs soil, sand and clay quickly.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Knap a shovel head from flint.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-knapping\">knapping guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-stone-shov": "Craft Shovel",
	"quest-stone-shov-desc": "With a shovel you can gather building soil and dig for clay.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Put the shovel head and a stick together in the crafting grid.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-starterguide\">starter guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-stone-dirt": "Collect Dirt for a House",
	"quest-stone-dirt-desc": "Soil is the quickest wall material you have.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Dig sixteen soil blocks with the shovel.<br><br><strong>Tip:</strong> Dig away from your camp so you do not leave pits to fall into.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-starterguide\">starter guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-stone-packed": "Craft Packed Dirt",
	"quest-stone-packed-desc": "Packed dirt is a firmer, neater building block than loose soil.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Craft packed dirt from soil in the crafting grid. Carry eight.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-starterguide\">starter guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-stone-shelter": "Build Your First Shelter",
	"quest-stone-shelter-desc": "A closed room keeps you warm, slows food spoiling and keeps monsters out.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Build walls and a roof with no gaps and add a door. Stand inside and the game sees the room.<br><br><strong>Tip:</strong> A small room warms up faster than a large one.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-starterguide\">starter guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"chapter-stone": "Stone Age",
	"quest-clay-clay": "Find Clay",
	"quest-clay-clay-desc": "Clay opens up pots, storage, moulds and bricks.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Look for blue or red clay patches near water or under grass and dig sixteen with a shovel.<br><br><strong>Tip:</strong> Fire clay is rarer and found under coal or in certain rock. You need it later.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-clayforming\">clay forming guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-clay-brick": "Make Bricks and Roof Shingles",
	"quest-clay-brick-desc": "Raw bricks and shingles become fireproof building material once fired.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Sneak and right-click the ground with clay to start clay forming, then pick the brick or shingle and fill in the shape layer by layer.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-clayforming\">clay forming guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-clay-storage": "Storage",
	"quest-clay-storage-desc": "A storage vessel keeps food fresh far longer than a basket.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Clay form a storage vessel. It must be fired in a pit kiln before use.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://gamemechanicinfo-foodpreservation\">food preservation guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-clay-cook": "Early Cooking",
	"quest-clay-cook-desc": "A cooking pot lets you make real meals from several ingredients.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Clay form a cooking pot. It must be fired before use.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-mealcooking\">meal cooking guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-clay-bowl": "Bowls",
	"quest-clay-bowl-desc": "Meals are served and eaten from bowls.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Clay form a bowl. One lump of clay makes several at once. Fire them before use.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-clayforming\">clay forming guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-clay-crock": "Crocks",
	"quest-clay-crock-desc": "A crock stores a cooked meal for weeks.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Clay form a crock and fire it.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://gamemechanicinfo-foodpreservation\">food preservation guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-clay-kiln-0": "Build a pit kiln",
	"quest-clay-kiln": "Pit Kilns",
	"quest-clay-kiln-desc": "A pit kiln fires raw clay into hard pottery.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Dig a hole one block deep, place the raw clay items in it, cover with dry grass, then sticks, then firewood, and light it.<br><br><strong>Tip:</strong> It burns for about a day. Keep grass and wood away from it.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-clayforming\">clay forming guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-clay-firebrick": "Fire Your Bricks",
	"quest-clay-firebrick-desc": "Fired bricks build ovens, chimneys and strong walls.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Fire your raw bricks in a pit kiln and collect them when it has burned out.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-clayforming\">clay forming guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-clay-moulds": "Crucible and Moulds",
	"quest-clay-moulds-desc": "A crucible and moulds are how metal is melted and cast.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Clay form a crucible and at least one tool mould, then fire them in a pit kiln.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-clayforming\">clay forming guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-clay-farm": "Farming",
	"quest-clay-farm-desc": "A watering can keeps crops alive in dry weather.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Clay form a watering can and fire it. Fill it at any water.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-clayforming\">clay forming guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-clay-liquid": "Liquids",
	"quest-clay-liquid-desc": "A jug carries water, milk and juice.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Clay form a jug and fire it.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-clayforming\">clay forming guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-clay-camp": "Campfire Cooking",
	"quest-clay-camp-desc": "The fired cooking pot goes on the fire pit.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Take the fired cooking pot from the kiln and carry it to your fire.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-mealcooking\">meal cooking guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-clay-cstore": "Clay Storage",
	"quest-clay-cstore-desc": "Fired storage vessels are your pantry.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Take the fired storage vessel from the kiln and place it somewhere cool.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://gamemechanicinfo-foodpreservation\">food preservation guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-clay-store-0": "Look at a container with food in it",
	"quest-clay-store": "Storing Food",
	"quest-clay-store-desc": "Food spoils. Good storage slows it down.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Put food into a storage vessel, then look at the vessel. Grain, vegetables and cured meat keep best.<br><br><strong>Tip:</strong> A vessel in a cellar keeps food longest.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://gamemechanicinfo-foodpreservation\">food preservation guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-clay-fclay": "Fire Clay",
	"quest-clay-fclay-desc": "Fire clay withstands great heat. Ovens and bloomeries need it.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Find fire clay under coal seams or in bauxite and dig some up.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-clayforming\">clay forming guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-clay-oven": "Form a Clay Oven",
	"quest-clay-oven-desc": "A clay oven bakes bread and pies.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Clay form a clay oven from fire clay.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-clayforming\">clay forming guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-clay-setup-0": "Place a clay oven",
	"quest-clay-setup": "Set Up Clay Oven",
	"quest-clay-setup-desc": "The oven has to be fired and placed before it bakes.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Fire the oven in a pit kiln, place it, and burn firewood inside to heat it.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-clayforming\">clay forming guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"chapter-clay": "Clay Working",
	"objective-line-copper-surface-0": "Have a copper nugget",
	"quest-copper-surface": "Find Surface Copper",
	"quest-copper-surface-desc": "Copper is the first metal. Small nuggets lie on the surface above ore.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Look for green or reddish stones on the ground and pick one up. Where they lie, ore sits below.<br><br><strong>Tip:</strong> Mark the spot on your map.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-smelting\">smelting guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-copper-pan": "Make a Pan",
	"quest-copper-pan-desc": "A pan washes metal out of sand and gravel.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Craft a wooden pan from a log in the crafting grid.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://gamemechanicinfo-panning\">panning guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-copper-panning-1": "Have a copper nugget",
	"quest-copper-panning": "Pan for Copper",
	"quest-copper-panning-desc": "Panning turns sand and gravel into nuggets, with patience.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Hold the pan, fill it at a sand or gravel block, then stand in water and hold the right mouse button. Have a copper nugget on you.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://gamemechanicinfo-panning\">panning guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-copper-nuggets-0": "Have 20 × copper nuggets",
	"quest-copper-nuggets": "Gather Copper Nuggets",
	"quest-copper-nuggets-desc": "Twenty nuggets make one ingot's worth of copper.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Collect twenty copper nuggets by panning, picking up surface stones, or digging under them.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-smelting\">smelting guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-copper-pit-0": "Build a charcoal pit",
	"quest-copper-pit": "Dig a Charcoal Pit",
	"quest-copper-pit-desc": "Charcoal burns hot enough to melt copper. Firewood does not.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Dig a pit, stack it full of firewood, light it and quickly cover the top with soil so it smoulders.<br><br><strong>Tip:</strong> Leave no gaps or the wood simply burns away.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-charcoalburning\">charcoal burning guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-copper-charcoal": "Burn Charcoal",
	"quest-copper-charcoal-desc": "Charcoal is the fuel of the whole metal age.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Wait for the charcoal pit to finish, then dig out the charcoal. Carry eight.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-charcoalburning\">charcoal burning guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-copper-smelt-0": "Have anything cast from copper",
	"quest-copper-smelt": "Smelt Copper",
	"quest-copper-smelt-desc": "Smelting turns nuggets into liquid metal for casting.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Put the nuggets in a fired crucible, set it on a fire pit with charcoal, and wait until the copper melts. Pour it into a mould.<br><br><strong>Tip:</strong> Carry the crucible with tongs or it burns you.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-smelting\">smelting guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-copper-tools-0": "Have a fired crucible",
	"objective-line-copper-tools-1": "Have a fired tool mould",
	"quest-copper-tools": "Cast Your First Tools",
	"quest-copper-tools-desc": "Cast copper tools last far longer than stone ones.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Finish the quests that lead here. Then carry a fired crucible and a fired tool mould.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-smelting\">smelting guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-copper-pickaxe-0": "Have a copper pickaxe or its head",
	"quest-copper-pickaxe": "Cast a Pickaxe",
	"quest-copper-pickaxe-desc": "A pickaxe mines stone and ore.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Pour copper into a pickaxe mould, let it cool, and put the head on a stick.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-smelting\">smelting guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-copper-mine-0": "Have copper ore",
	"quest-copper-mine": "Mine Copper Ore",
	"quest-copper-mine-desc": "Ore in the rock gives far more metal than surface nuggets.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Dig down under surface copper until you reach the ore and mine a block with the pickaxe.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-smelting\">smelting guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-copper-propick-0": "Have a copper prospecting pick or its head",
	"quest-copper-propick": "Cast a Prospecting Pick",
	"quest-copper-propick-desc": "A prospecting pick tells you which ores are nearby.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Cast a prospecting pick head and put it on a stick.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://gamemechanicinfo-prospecting\">prospecting guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-copper-prospect-0": "Take a reading with a prospecting pick",
	"quest-copper-prospect": "Prospect for Ore",
	"quest-copper-prospect-desc": "Prospecting saves you digging blind.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Break a stone block with the prospecting pick and read the report in the chat.<br><br><strong>Tip:</strong> Take three samples close together for the first reading.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://gamemechanicinfo-prospecting\">prospecting guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-copper-hammer-0": "Have a copper hammer or its head",
	"quest-copper-hammer": "Cast a Hammer",
	"quest-copper-hammer-desc": "A hammer is needed for smithing and for crushing ore.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Cast a hammer head and put it on a stick.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-smithing\">smithing guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-copper-axe-0": "Have a copper axe or its head",
	"quest-copper-axe": "Cast an Axe",
	"quest-copper-axe-desc": "A copper axe fells trees much faster.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Cast an axe head and put it on a stick.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-smelting\">smelting guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-copper-knife-0": "Have a copper knife or its blade",
	"quest-copper-knife": "Cast a Knife Blade",
	"quest-copper-knife-desc": "A copper knife butchers faster.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Cast a knife blade and put it on a stick.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-smelting\">smelting guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-copper-shovel-0": "Have a copper shovel or its head",
	"quest-copper-shovel": "Cast a Shovel",
	"quest-copper-shovel-desc": "A copper shovel digs faster and lasts longer.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Cast a shovel head and put it on a stick.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-smelting\">smelting guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-copper-hoe-0": "Have a copper hoe or its head",
	"quest-copper-hoe": "Cast a Hoe",
	"quest-copper-hoe-desc": "A copper hoe tills more land before it wears out.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Cast a hoe head and put it on a stick.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-smelting\">smelting guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-copper-ingots": "Cast Copper Ingots",
	"quest-copper-ingots-desc": "Ingots are metal in the shape smithing needs.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Pour molten copper into an ingot mould. Carry four ingots.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-smithing\">smithing guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-copper-anvil": "Cast an Anvil",
	"quest-copper-anvil-desc": "An anvil is where ingots are hammered into shape.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Cast a copper anvil in an anvil mould. It takes a lot of copper. Set it down in the world to finish the quest.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-smithing\">smithing guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-copper-forge": "Build a Forge",
	"quest-copper-forge-desc": "A forge heats ingots until they can be worked.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Build a forge from stones and place it near the anvil. Fuel it with charcoal or coal. Set it down in the world to finish the quest.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-smithing\">smithing guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-copper-smith-0": "Stand at an anvil",
	"objective-line-copper-smith-1": "Stand at a forge",
	"objective-line-copper-smith-2": "Have a hammer",
	"objective-line-copper-smith-3": "Have a copper ingot",
	"quest-copper-smith": "Start Smithing",
	"quest-copper-smith-desc": "Smithing makes the parts that cannot be cast.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Finish the quests that lead here. Then stand at your anvil and forge with a hammer and a copper ingot on you.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-smithing\">smithing guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-copper-saw-0": "Have a copper saw or its blade",
	"quest-copper-saw": "Smith a Saw",
	"quest-copper-saw-desc": "A saw cuts logs into boards. Carpentry starts here.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Heat an ingot in the forge, place it on the anvil, pick the saw blade and hammer it into shape. Put it on a stick.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-smithing\">smithing guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-copper-shears": "Smith Shears",
	"quest-copper-shears-desc": "Shears cut leaves and shear sheep.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Smith shears on the anvil.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-smithing\">smithing guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-copper-scythe-0": "Have a copper scythe or its blade",
	"quest-copper-scythe": "Smith a Scythe",
	"quest-copper-scythe-desc": "A scythe harvests a wide swathe of grass or crops in one swing.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Smith a scythe blade and put it on a stick.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-smithing\">smithing guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-copper-chisel-0": "Have a copper chisel",
	"quest-copper-chisel": "Smith a Chisel",
	"quest-copper-chisel-desc": "A chisel carves blocks into fine shapes.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Smith a chisel on the anvil.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-smithing\">smithing guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-copper-armour-0": "Have a piece of copper armour",
	"quest-copper-armour": "Smith Copper Armour",
	"quest-copper-armour-desc": "Copper armour is your first real protection.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Smith plates, scales or chain and craft them into a piece of copper armour.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-armor\">armor guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-copper-master": "Master Coppersmith",
	"quest-copper-master-desc": "You have worked copper from the first nugget to finished tools.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Finish the quests that lead here, then claim it.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-smelting\">smelting guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-copper-tongs": "Make Tongs",
	"quest-copper-tongs-desc": "Tongs let you handle hot crucibles and ingots.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Craft wooden tongs from sticks in the crafting grid.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-smelting\">smelting guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-copper-coal-0": "Have coal",
	"quest-copper-coal": "Find Coal",
	"quest-copper-coal-desc": "Coal burns hotter and longer than charcoal.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Find a seam of brown or black coal, often in sedimentary rock, and mine some.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-charcoalburning\">charcoal burning guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-copper-moulds": "Form Tool Moulds",
	"quest-copper-moulds-desc": "Each tool needs its own mould.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Clay form the moulds you want and fire them in a pit kiln.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-smelting\">smelting guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-copper-breakore-0": "Have 40 × copper nuggets",
	"quest-copper-breakore": "Break Up Ore",
	"quest-copper-breakore-desc": "Mined ore has to be broken up before it can be smelted.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Place the ore chunks and strike them with a hammer, or craft them with a hammer. Carry forty nuggets.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-smelting\">smelting guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-copper-digmine": "Dig a Mine",
	"quest-copper-digmine-desc": "A proper mine goes down to where the ore is.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Dig a safe way down, with ladders or stairs, until you are fifteen blocks below sea level.<br><br><strong>Tip:</strong> Bring torches and prop up loose ground.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://gamemechanicinfo-prospecting\">prospecting guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-copper-tin": "Find Tin",
	"quest-copper-tin-desc": "Tin mixed with copper makes bronze.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Find cassiterite. Its surface stones are dark, and it is rarer than copper. Have a nugget on you.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://gamemechanicinfo-prospecting\">prospecting guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-copper-falx-0": "Have a copper falx or its blade",
	"quest-copper-falx": "Cast a Falx Blade",
	"quest-copper-falx-desc": "The falx is a simple curved blade and a good first weapon.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Cast a falx blade and put it on a stick.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-smelting\">smelting guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-copper-spear-0": "Have a copper spear or its head",
	"quest-copper-spear": "Cast a Spear Head",
	"quest-copper-spear-desc": "A copper spear hits harder and flies truer.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Cast a spear head and put it on a stick.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-smelting\">smelting guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-copper-nails": "Smith Nails and Strips",
	"quest-copper-nails-desc": "Nails and strips hold chests, doors and barrels together.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Smith nails and strips from a copper ingot.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-smithing\">smithing guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-copper-plates": "Smith Copper Plates",
	"quest-copper-plates-desc": "Metal plates go into lanterns, armour and machines.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Smith a copper plate. It takes two ingots.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-smithing\">smithing guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-copper-arrowheads": "Smith Arrowheads",
	"quest-copper-arrowheads-desc": "Metal arrowheads make arrows that pierce.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Smith arrowheads from a copper ingot.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-smithing\">smithing guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-copper-lantern": "Make a Copper Lantern",
	"quest-copper-lantern-desc": "A lantern is a safe light that never burns out.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Craft a lantern from a copper plate, glass or not, and a candle. Carry it.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-smelting\">smelting guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"chapter-copper": "Copper Age",
	"objective-line-bronze-tinnug-0": "Have 20 × tin nuggets",
	"quest-bronze-tinnug": "Gather Tin Nuggets",
	"quest-bronze-tinnug-desc": "A batch of bronze needs about one part tin to nine parts copper.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Break cassiterite ore into nuggets with a hammer and carry twenty.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-smelting\">smelting guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-bronze-tinbronze-0": "Have anything made of tin bronze",
	"quest-bronze-tinbronze": "Alloy Tin Bronze",
	"quest-bronze-tinbronze-desc": "Tin bronze is the standard bronze and the easiest to make.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Put copper and tin nuggets in a crucible, with tin between 8 and 12 of every 100, and melt them in a firepit. Pour it and carry anything made of tin bronze.<br><br><strong>Tip:</strong> The crucible window shows the alloy it will make before you light the fire.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-smelting\">smelting guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-bronze-gold-0": "Have gold ore or a gold nugget",
	"quest-bronze-gold": "Find Gold",
	"quest-bronze-gold-desc": "Gold is one of the two metals that turn copper into black bronze.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Look for gold in quartz veins, or pan for it. Carry gold ore or a gold nugget.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://gamemechanicinfo-prospecting\">prospecting guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-bronze-silver-0": "Have silver ore or a silver nugget",
	"quest-bronze-silver": "Find Silver",
	"quest-bronze-silver-desc": "Silver is the other metal for black bronze.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Look for silver in quartz veins and with galena. Carry silver ore or a silver nugget.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://gamemechanicinfo-prospecting\">prospecting guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-bronze-blackbronze-0": "Have anything made of black bronze",
	"quest-bronze-blackbronze": "Alloy Black Bronze",
	"quest-bronze-blackbronze-desc": "Black bronze is the strongest of the three bronzes.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Melt copper with gold and silver, each between 8 and 16 of every 100. Carry anything made of black bronze.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-smelting\">smelting guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-bronze-bism-0": "Have bismuthinite ore or a nugget",
	"quest-bronze-bism": "Find Bismuth",
	"quest-bronze-bism-desc": "Bismuth makes a bronze where there is no tin to be found.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Prospect for bismuthinite and carry a piece of the ore or a nugget.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://gamemechanicinfo-prospecting\">prospecting guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-bronze-zinc-0": "Have sphalerite ore or a nugget",
	"quest-bronze-zinc": "Find Zinc",
	"quest-bronze-zinc-desc": "Zinc comes from sphalerite. It goes into bismuth bronze and brass.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Prospect for sphalerite and carry a piece of the ore or a nugget.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://gamemechanicinfo-prospecting\">prospecting guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-bronze-bisbronze-0": "Have anything made of bismuth bronze",
	"quest-bronze-bisbronze": "Alloy Bismuth Bronze",
	"quest-bronze-bisbronze-desc": "Bismuth bronze is softer than tin bronze, but it works.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Melt copper with bismuth (10 to 20 of every 100) and zinc (20 to 30 of every 100). Carry anything made of bismuth bronze.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-smelting\">smelting guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-bronze-brass-0": "Have anything made of brass",
	"quest-bronze-brass": "Make Brass",
	"quest-bronze-brass-desc": "Brass is copper and zinc. It is for fittings and decoration, not tools.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Melt copper with zinc, between 30 and 40 of every 100. Carry anything made of brass.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-smelting\">smelting guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-bronze-bronze-0": "Have anything made of bronze",
	"quest-bronze-bronze": "Pour Your First Bronze",
	"quest-bronze-bronze-desc": "Any one of the three bronzes opens the Bronze Age.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Finish one of the alloy quests, then carry anything made of bronze.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-smelting\">smelting guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-bronze-tools-0": "Have a fired tool mould",
	"objective-line-bronze-tools-1": "Have a bronze ingot",
	"quest-bronze-tools": "Cast Bronze Tools",
	"quest-bronze-tools-desc": "Bronze tools last far longer than copper and dig harder stone.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Finish the quests that lead here. Then carry a fired tool mould and a bronze ingot.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-smelting\">smelting guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-bronze-pickaxe-0": "Have a bronze pickaxe or its head",
	"quest-bronze-pickaxe": "Cast a Bronze Pickaxe",
	"quest-bronze-pickaxe-desc": "A bronze pickaxe can mine iron ore.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Fill a pickaxe mould with molten bronze from the crucible, let it cool, and take it out. The head alone counts, or the finished tool.<br><br><strong>Tip:</strong> This is the tool that opens the Iron Age.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-smelting\">smelting guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-bronze-iron-0": "Have iron ore or an iron nugget",
	"quest-bronze-iron": "Mine Iron Ore",
	"quest-bronze-iron-desc": "Iron ore is the next step up from bronze.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Mine limonite, hematite or magnetite with a bronze pickaxe. Carry a piece of the ore or a nugget.<br><br><strong>Tip:</strong> Limonite is the most common. Look for it under bogs and in shallow rock.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://gamemechanicinfo-prospecting\">prospecting guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-bronze-propick-0": "Have a bronze prospecting pick or its head",
	"quest-bronze-propick": "Cast a Bronze Prospecting Pick",
	"quest-bronze-propick-desc": "A bronze prospecting pick lasts through many more readings.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Fill a prospecting pick mould with molten bronze from the crucible, let it cool, and take it out. The head alone counts, or the finished tool.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://gamemechanicinfo-prospecting\">prospecting guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-bronze-deep-0": "Take 5 readings with a bronze prospecting pick",
	"quest-bronze-deep": "Prospect Deeper",
	"quest-bronze-deep-desc": "The metals you need next lie deeper and are spread thin.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Take five readings with a bronze prospecting pick.<br><br><strong>Tip:</strong> Write the readings on your map so you can compare places.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://gamemechanicinfo-prospecting\">prospecting guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-bronze-hammer-0": "Have a bronze hammer or its head",
	"quest-bronze-hammer": "Cast a Bronze Hammer",
	"quest-bronze-hammer-desc": "A hammer works metal on the anvil and breaks ore into nuggets.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Fill a hammer mould with molten bronze from the crucible, let it cool, and take it out. The head alone counts, or the finished tool.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-smithing\">smithing guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-bronze-axe-0": "Have a bronze axe or its head",
	"quest-bronze-axe": "Cast a Bronze Axe",
	"quest-bronze-axe-desc": "A bronze axe fells trees faster.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Fill a axe mould with molten bronze from the crucible, let it cool, and take it out. The head alone counts, or the finished tool.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-smelting\">smelting guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-bronze-knife-0": "Have a bronze knife or its blade",
	"quest-bronze-knife": "Cast a Bronze Knife",
	"quest-bronze-knife-desc": "A bronze knife butchers faster and lasts longer.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Fill a knife blade mould with molten bronze from the crucible, let it cool, and take it out. The head alone counts, or the finished tool.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-smelting\">smelting guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-bronze-shovel-0": "Have a bronze shovel or its head",
	"quest-bronze-shovel": "Cast a Bronze Shovel",
	"quest-bronze-shovel-desc": "A bronze shovel makes short work of soil, sand and gravel.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Fill a shovel mould with molten bronze from the crucible, let it cool, and take it out. The head alone counts, or the finished tool.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-smelting\">smelting guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-bronze-hoe-0": "Have a bronze hoe or its head",
	"quest-bronze-hoe": "Cast a Bronze Hoe",
	"quest-bronze-hoe-desc": "A bronze hoe will till a whole season of fields.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Fill a hoe mould with molten bronze from the crucible, let it cool, and take it out. The head alone counts, or the finished tool.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-smelting\">smelting guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-bronze-falx-0": "Have a bronze falx or its blade",
	"quest-bronze-falx": "Cast a Bronze Falx",
	"quest-bronze-falx-desc": "The falx is a curved blade and a strong hand weapon.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Fill a falx blade mould with molten bronze from the crucible, let it cool, and take it out. The head alone counts, or the finished tool.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-smelting\">smelting guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-bronze-spear-0": "Have a bronze spear or its head",
	"quest-bronze-spear": "Cast a Bronze Spear",
	"quest-bronze-spear-desc": "A bronze spear hits harder and can still be thrown.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Fill a spear head mould with molten bronze from the crucible, let it cool, and take it out. The head alone counts, or the finished tool.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-smelting\">smelting guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-bronze-ingots-0": "Have 4 × bronze ingots",
	"quest-bronze-ingots": "Cast Bronze Ingots",
	"quest-bronze-ingots-desc": "Ingots are how metal is stored and worked.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Pour molten bronze into ingot moulds and carry four ingots of any bronze.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-smithing\">smithing guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-bronze-anvil-0": "Place a bronze anvil",
	"quest-bronze-anvil": "Cast a Bronze Anvil",
	"quest-bronze-anvil-desc": "Iron can only be worked on a bronze anvil or better.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Cast a bronze anvil in an anvil mould. It takes a lot of bronze. Set it down in the world to finish the quest.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-smithing\">smithing guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-bronze-smith-0": "Stand at a bronze anvil",
	"objective-line-bronze-smith-1": "Stand at a forge",
	"objective-line-bronze-smith-2": "Have a hammer",
	"objective-line-bronze-smith-3": "Have a bronze ingot",
	"quest-bronze-smith": "Smith in Bronze",
	"quest-bronze-smith-desc": "With a bronze anvil you can smith what cannot be cast.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Finish the quests that lead here. Then stand at your bronze anvil and forge with a hammer and a bronze ingot on you.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-smithing\">smithing guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-bronze-saw-0": "Have a bronze saw or its blade",
	"quest-bronze-saw": "Smith a Bronze Saw",
	"quest-bronze-saw-desc": "A bronze saw cuts many more boards before it wears out.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Heat bronze in the forge, lay it on the anvil, pick the saw blade, and hammer it into shape.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-smithing\">smithing guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-bronze-chisel-0": "Have a bronze chisel",
	"quest-bronze-chisel": "Smith a Bronze Chisel",
	"quest-bronze-chisel-desc": "A chisel carves stone and wood into finer shapes.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Heat bronze in the forge, lay it on the anvil, pick the chisel, and hammer it into shape.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-smithing\">smithing guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-bronze-shears-0": "Have bronze shears",
	"quest-bronze-shears": "Smith Bronze Shears",
	"quest-bronze-shears-desc": "Bronze shears take cuttings and clip leaves.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Heat bronze in the forge, lay it on the anvil, pick the shear blades, and hammer it into shape.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-smithing\">smithing guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-bronze-scythe-0": "Have a bronze scythe or its blade",
	"quest-bronze-scythe": "Smith a Bronze Scythe",
	"quest-bronze-scythe-desc": "A bronze scythe harvests a field in a few swings.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Heat bronze in the forge, lay it on the anvil, pick the scythe blade, and hammer it into shape.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-smithing\">smithing guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-bronze-plates-0": "Have a bronze plate",
	"quest-bronze-plates": "Smith Bronze Plates",
	"quest-bronze-plates-desc": "Plates go into lanterns, armour and machines.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Heat bronze in the forge, lay it on the anvil, pick the plate, and hammer it into shape.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-smithing\">smithing guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-bronze-lantern": "Make a Bronze Lantern",
	"quest-bronze-lantern-desc": "A lantern gives steady light and never burns out.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Craft a lantern from a bronze plate and a candle or oil lamp, with glass if you have it. Carry it.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-smelting\">smelting guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-bronze-chain-0": "Have bronze chain",
	"quest-bronze-chain": "Smith Bronze Chain",
	"quest-bronze-chain-desc": "Chain is the material for chain armour.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Heat bronze in the forge, lay it on the anvil, pick the chain, and hammer it into shape.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-smithing\">smithing guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-bronze-chainarm-0": "Have a piece of bronze chain armour",
	"quest-bronze-chainarm": "Bronze Chain Armour",
	"quest-bronze-chainarm-desc": "Chain armour stops blades and still lets you move.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Craft any piece of bronze chain armour from chain and leather.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-armor\">armor guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-bronze-scales-0": "Have bronze scales",
	"quest-bronze-scales": "Smith Bronze Scales",
	"quest-bronze-scales-desc": "Scales are sewn onto leather to make scale armour.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Heat bronze in the forge, lay it on the anvil, pick the scales, and hammer it into shape.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-smithing\">smithing guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-bronze-scalearm-0": "Have a piece of bronze scale armour",
	"quest-bronze-scalearm": "Bronze Scale Armour",
	"quest-bronze-scalearm-desc": "Scale armour protects better than chain but is heavier.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Craft any piece of bronze scale armour from scales and leather.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-armor\">armor guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-bronze-arrow-0": "Have bronze arrowheads",
	"quest-bronze-arrow": "Smith Bronze Arrowheads",
	"quest-bronze-arrow-desc": "Bronze arrowheads fly true and hit hard.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Heat bronze in the forge, lay it on the anvil, pick arrowheads, and hammer it into shape.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-smithing\">smithing guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-bronze-master": "Master Bronzesmith",
	"quest-bronze-master-desc": "You have found the ores, mixed the alloys, cast the tools and worked the anvil.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Finish the quests that lead here, then claim it.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-smelting\">smelting guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"chapter-bronze": "Bronze Age",
	"objective-line-iron-crush-0": "Have 20 × iron nuggets",
	"quest-iron-crush": "Break Up Iron Ore",
	"quest-iron-crush-desc": "A bloomery is fed with nuggets, not whole ore.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Break iron ore with a hammer and carry twenty nuggets.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-smelting\">smelting guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-iron-fireclay": "Find Fire Clay",
	"quest-iron-fireclay-desc": "Fire clay stands heat that would crack ordinary clay.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Dig fire clay, often found under coal, or make it by mixing clay with crushed flint. Carry some.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-smelting\">smelting guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-iron-bloomery-0": "Build a bloomery",
	"quest-iron-bloomery": "Build a Bloomery",
	"quest-iron-bloomery-desc": "A bloomery burns hot enough to turn iron ore into a bloom.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Form a bloomery base and chimney from fire clay and set the chimney on the base.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-smelting\">smelting guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-iron-fuel": "Stock Up on Charcoal",
	"quest-iron-fuel-desc": "Each load of iron needs as much charcoal as ore.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Burn charcoal in pits and carry forty pieces.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-smelting\">smelting guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-iron-bloom": "Smelt an Iron Bloom",
	"quest-iron-bloom-desc": "The bloomery gives a spongy lump of iron called a bloom.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Fill the bloomery with iron nuggets and charcoal, light it, and wait until it burns out. Break the base open to take the bloom.<br><br><strong>Tip:</strong> Rebuild the base afterwards. The chimney is not harmed.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-smelting\">smelting guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-iron-work": "Work the Bloom",
	"quest-iron-work-desc": "A bloom is full of slag that must be hammered out.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Heat the bloom in the forge and work it on a bronze anvil until an iron ingot is left.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-smithing\">smithing guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-iron-flux-0": "Have powdered borax",
	"quest-iron-flux": "Find Borax for Flux",
	"quest-iron-flux-desc": "Borax lets two pieces of hot iron weld into one.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Find borax in dry lands and grind it to a powder in a quern. Carry some.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-smithing\">smithing guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-iron-ianvil": "Smith an Iron Anvil",
	"quest-iron-ianvil-desc": "An iron anvil is needed to work steel.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Smith the two halves of an iron anvil, then weld them together with borax. Set it down in the world to finish the quest.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-smithing\">smithing guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-iron-tools-0": "Stand at an anvil",
	"objective-line-iron-tools-1": "Stand at a forge",
	"objective-line-iron-tools-2": "Have a hammer",
	"objective-line-iron-tools-3": "Have an iron ingot",
	"quest-iron-tools": "Smith Iron Tools",
	"quest-iron-tools-desc": "Iron cannot be cast. Every iron tool is hammered out on the anvil.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Finish the quests that lead here. Then stand at your anvil and forge with a hammer and an iron ingot on you.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-smithing\">smithing guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-iron-arms-0": "Stand at an anvil",
	"objective-line-iron-arms-1": "Stand at a forge",
	"objective-line-iron-arms-2": "Have a hammer",
	"objective-line-iron-arms-3": "Have 2 × iron ingots",
	"quest-iron-arms": "Smith Iron Arms",
	"quest-iron-arms-desc": "Iron weapons and armour will see a colony through its hardest fights.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Finish the quests that lead here. Then stand at your anvil and forge with a hammer and two iron ingots on you.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-smithing\">smithing guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-iron-pickaxe-0": "Have an iron pickaxe or its head",
	"quest-iron-pickaxe": "Smith an Iron Pickaxe",
	"quest-iron-pickaxe-desc": "An iron pickaxe mines every ore there is.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Heat an iron ingot in the forge, lay it on the anvil, pick the pickaxe head, and hammer it into shape.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-smithing\">smithing guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-iron-propick-0": "Have an iron prospecting pick or its head",
	"quest-iron-propick": "Smith an Iron Prospecting Pick",
	"quest-iron-propick-desc": "An iron prospecting pick will last for many journeys.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Heat an iron ingot in the forge, lay it on the anvil, pick the prospecting pick head, and hammer it into shape.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://gamemechanicinfo-prospecting\">prospecting guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-iron-hammer-0": "Have an iron hammer or its head",
	"quest-iron-hammer": "Smith an Iron Hammer",
	"quest-iron-hammer-desc": "An iron hammer is the smith's own tool.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Heat an iron ingot in the forge, lay it on the anvil, pick the hammer head, and hammer it into shape.<br><br><strong>Tip:</strong> Later a helve hammer, driven by a windmill, can do the hammering for you.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-smithing\">smithing guide</a> and the <a href=\"handbook://gamemechanicinfo-mechanicalpower\">mechanical power guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-iron-axe-0": "Have an iron axe or its head",
	"quest-iron-axe": "Smith an Iron Axe",
	"quest-iron-axe-desc": "An iron axe brings down the largest trees.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Heat an iron ingot in the forge, lay it on the anvil, pick the axe head, and hammer it into shape.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-smithing\">smithing guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-iron-knife-0": "Have an iron knife or its blade",
	"quest-iron-knife": "Smith an Iron Knife",
	"quest-iron-knife-desc": "An iron knife stays sharp for a long time.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Heat an iron ingot in the forge, lay it on the anvil, pick the knife blade, and hammer it into shape.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-smithing\">smithing guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-iron-shovel-0": "Have an iron shovel or its head",
	"quest-iron-shovel": "Smith an Iron Shovel",
	"quest-iron-shovel-desc": "An iron shovel digs fast and lasts.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Heat an iron ingot in the forge, lay it on the anvil, pick the shovel head, and hammer it into shape.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-smithing\">smithing guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-iron-hoe-0": "Have an iron hoe or its head",
	"quest-iron-hoe": "Smith an Iron Hoe",
	"quest-iron-hoe-desc": "An iron hoe will till fields for years.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Heat an iron ingot in the forge, lay it on the anvil, pick the hoe head, and hammer it into shape.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-smithing\">smithing guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-iron-saw-0": "Have an iron saw or its blade",
	"quest-iron-saw": "Smith an Iron Saw",
	"quest-iron-saw-desc": "An iron saw is the carpenter's best tool.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Heat an iron ingot in the forge, lay it on the anvil, pick the saw blade, and hammer it into shape.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-smithing\">smithing guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-iron-scythe-0": "Have an iron scythe or its blade",
	"quest-iron-scythe": "Smith an Iron Scythe",
	"quest-iron-scythe-desc": "An iron scythe clears a field in moments.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Heat an iron ingot in the forge, lay it on the anvil, pick the scythe blade, and hammer it into shape.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-smithing\">smithing guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-iron-falx-0": "Have an iron falx or its blade",
	"quest-iron-falx": "Smith an Iron Falx",
	"quest-iron-falx-desc": "An iron falx is a fearsome blade.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Heat an iron ingot in the forge, lay it on the anvil, pick the falx blade, and hammer it into shape.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-smithing\">smithing guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-iron-spear-0": "Have an iron spear or its head",
	"quest-iron-spear": "Smith an Iron Spear",
	"quest-iron-spear-desc": "An iron spear is strong in the hand and in the air.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Heat an iron ingot in the forge, lay it on the anvil, pick the spear head, and hammer it into shape.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-smithing\">smithing guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-iron-arrow-0": "Have iron arrowheads",
	"quest-iron-arrow": "Smith Iron Arrowheads",
	"quest-iron-arrow-desc": "Iron arrowheads pierce what bronze will not.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Heat an iron ingot in the forge, lay it on the anvil, pick arrowheads, and hammer it into shape.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-smithing\">smithing guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-iron-chain-0": "Have iron chain",
	"quest-iron-chain": "Smith Iron Chain",
	"quest-iron-chain-desc": "Iron chain is the material for iron chain armour.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Heat an iron ingot in the forge, lay it on the anvil, pick the chain, and hammer it into shape.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-smithing\">smithing guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-iron-chainarm-0": "Have a piece of iron chain armour",
	"quest-iron-chainarm": "Iron Chain Armour",
	"quest-iron-chainarm-desc": "Iron chain armour is a solid, flexible defence.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Craft any piece of iron chain armour from chain and leather.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-armor\">armor guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-iron-scales-0": "Have iron scales",
	"quest-iron-scales": "Smith Iron Scales",
	"quest-iron-scales-desc": "Iron scales make a heavier, tougher armour.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Heat an iron ingot in the forge, lay it on the anvil, pick the scales, and hammer it into shape.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-smithing\">smithing guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-iron-scalearm-0": "Have a piece of iron scale armour",
	"quest-iron-scalearm": "Iron Scale Armour",
	"quest-iron-scalearm-desc": "Iron scale armour turns most blows.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Craft any piece of iron scale armour from scales and leather.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-armor\">armor guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-iron-plates-0": "Have an iron plate",
	"quest-iron-plates": "Smith Iron Plates",
	"quest-iron-plates-desc": "Iron plates are the start of plate armour.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Heat an iron ingot in the forge, lay it on the anvil, pick the plate, and hammer it into shape.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-smithing\">smithing guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-iron-platearm-0": "Have a piece of iron plate armour",
	"quest-iron-platearm": "Iron Plate Armour",
	"quest-iron-platearm-desc": "Plate armour is the heaviest protection iron can give.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Craft any piece of iron plate armour.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-armor\">armor guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-iron-rbrick": "Fire Refractory Bricks",
	"quest-iron-rbrick-desc": "Refractory bricks line furnaces that must stay hot for days.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Form bricks from fire clay and fire them in a kiln. Carry some.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://gamemechanicinfo-steelmaking\">steel making guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-iron-fdoor-0": "Have an iron door",
	"quest-iron-fdoor": "Smith a Furnace Door",
	"quest-iron-fdoor-desc": "The cementation furnace is closed with an iron door.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Smith the furnace door from iron as the handbook shows.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://gamemechanicinfo-steelmaking\">steel making guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-iron-coffin-0": "Place a stone coffin",
	"quest-iron-coffin": "Carve a Stone Coffin",
	"quest-iron-coffin-desc": "The stone coffin holds the iron while it turns to steel.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Craft the two halves of a stone coffin and set them down end to end.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://gamemechanicinfo-steelmaking\">steel making guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-iron-furnace-0": "Place refractory bricks",
	"quest-iron-furnace": "Build a Cementation Furnace",
	"quest-iron-furnace-desc": "A cementation furnace bakes carbon into iron.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Build the furnace around the stone coffin from refractory bricks, with the door in front, as the handbook shows. Stand beside it.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://gamemechanicinfo-steelmaking\">steel making guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-iron-carb": "Carburise Iron",
	"quest-iron-carb-desc": "Iron packed in charcoal and baked for days becomes blister steel.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Fill the stone coffin with iron ingots and charcoal, close it with its lid, and keep the fire below it burning. Stand at the closed coffin.<br><br><strong>Tip:</strong> Coke burns hotter and longer than charcoal.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://gamemechanicinfo-steelmaking\">steel making guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-iron-blister": "Take Out Blister Steel",
	"quest-iron-blister-desc": "Blister steel is rough steel, named for the bubbles on its skin.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> When the furnace has cooled, open the coffin and take out the blister steel.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://gamemechanicinfo-steelmaking\">steel making guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-iron-steel": "Work It into Steel",
	"quest-iron-steel-desc": "Blister steel must be worked to even it out.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Heat blister steel in the forge and work it on an iron anvil until a steel ingot is left.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://gamemechanicinfo-steelmaking\">steel making guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-iron-sanvil": "Smith a Steel Anvil",
	"quest-iron-sanvil-desc": "A steel anvil is the last anvil you will ever need.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Smith the two halves of a steel anvil and weld them with borax. Set it down in the world to finish the quest.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://gamemechanicinfo-steelmaking\">steel making guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-iron-ssmith-0": "Stand at an iron or steel anvil",
	"objective-line-iron-ssmith-1": "Stand at a forge",
	"objective-line-iron-ssmith-2": "Have a hammer",
	"objective-line-iron-ssmith-3": "Have a steel ingot",
	"quest-iron-ssmith": "Smith in Steel",
	"quest-iron-ssmith-desc": "Steel is the best metal for tools and arms.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Finish the quests that lead here. Then stand at an iron or steel anvil and a forge with a hammer and a steel ingot on you.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://gamemechanicinfo-steelmaking\">steel making guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-iron-spick-0": "Have a steel pickaxe or its head",
	"quest-iron-spick": "Smith a Steel Pickaxe",
	"quest-iron-spick-desc": "A steel pickaxe outlasts every other.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Heat a steel ingot in the forge, lay it on the anvil, pick the pickaxe head, and hammer it into shape.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://gamemechanicinfo-steelmaking\">steel making guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-iron-saxe-0": "Have a steel axe or its head",
	"quest-iron-saxe": "Smith a Steel Axe",
	"quest-iron-saxe-desc": "A steel axe keeps its edge for a very long time.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Heat a steel ingot in the forge, lay it on the anvil, pick the axe head, and hammer it into shape.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://gamemechanicinfo-steelmaking\">steel making guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-iron-sfalx-0": "Have a steel falx or its blade",
	"quest-iron-sfalx": "Smith a Steel Falx",
	"quest-iron-sfalx-desc": "A steel falx is the finest blade you can make.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Heat a steel ingot in the forge, lay it on the anvil, pick the falx blade, and hammer it into shape.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://gamemechanicinfo-steelmaking\">steel making guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-iron-splates": "Smith Steel Plates",
	"quest-iron-splates-desc": "Steel plates make the best armour.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Heat a steel ingot in the forge, lay it on the anvil, pick the plate, and hammer it into shape.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://gamemechanicinfo-steelmaking\">steel making guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-iron-sarm-0": "Have a piece of steel plate armour",
	"quest-iron-sarm": "Steel Plate Armour",
	"quest-iron-sarm-desc": "Steel plate armour is the strongest armour there is.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Craft any piece of steel plate armour.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-armor\">armor guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-iron-master": "Master of Iron and Steel",
	"quest-iron-master-desc": "From bog ore to steel plate, you have mastered iron.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Finish the quests that lead here, then claim it.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-smithing\">smithing guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"chapter-iron": "Iron and Steel",
	"quest-kitchen-serve": "Serve Your First Meal",
	"quest-kitchen-serve-desc": "A cooked meal feeds you far better than raw food, and it fills several food groups at once.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Put a cooking pot on a firepit, add at least two of the same kind of food, and let it cook. Then right-click the pot with an empty bowl to take a serving.<br><br><strong>Tip:</strong> The bowl of food in your hands is what the quest looks for.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-mealcooking\">meal cooking guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-kitchen-eggs": "Cook Scrambled Eggs",
	"quest-kitchen-eggs-desc": "Scrambled eggs are a quick protein meal.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Cook two or more eggs in a cooking pot. You can add cheese or vegetables in the other slots. Take a serving in a bowl.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-mealcooking\">meal cooking guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-kitchen-soup": "Cook a Soup",
	"quest-kitchen-soup-desc": "Soup stretches a few vegetables into a filling meal.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Put a portion of water in the cooking pot with two or more vegetables, then cook it. Meat can go in the spare slots. Take a serving in a bowl.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-mealcooking\">meal cooking guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-kitchen-porridge": "Cook Porridge",
	"quest-kitchen-porridge-desc": "Porridge is the simplest grain meal and needs no quern.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Cook two or more portions of grain in a cooking pot. Fruit or honey can go in the spare slots. Take a serving in a bowl.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-mealcooking\">meal cooking guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-kitchen-stew": "Cook a Meaty Stew",
	"quest-kitchen-stew-desc": "Meaty stew is the best early source of protein.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Cook two or more pieces of meat in a cooking pot. Add vegetables or more meat in the spare slots. Take a serving in a bowl.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-mealcooking\">meal cooking guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-kitchen-vstew": "Cook a Vegetable Stew",
	"quest-kitchen-vstew-desc": "Vegetable stew is a full meal with no hunting needed.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Cook two or more vegetables in a cooking pot without water. Take a serving in a bowl.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-mealcooking\">meal cooking guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-kitchen-fullpot": "Cook a Full Pot",
	"quest-kitchen-fullpot-desc": "One pot can cook up to six servings in one go, which saves a lot of fuel.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Put six of each ingredient into the pot before you light the fire. Carry six servings of cooked meals in bowls or crocks.<br><br><strong>Tip:</strong> Crocks hold four servings each, so they are the easy way to carry this much.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-mealcooking\">meal cooking guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-kitchen-milk": "Fill a Bucket with Milk",
	"quest-kitchen-milk-desc": "Milk is the start of all cheese making.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Right-click a ewe, nanny goat or other milk animal with an empty bucket. She must have had young, and be calm enough to let you near. Carry it in a bucket, bowl or jug, or look at the barrel or pot that holds it.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-cheese\">cheese guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-kitchen-curdle": "Curdle Milk",
	"quest-kitchen-curdle-desc": "Curdled milk is the first step from milk to cheese.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Seal milk in a barrel with the curdling ingredient the handbook lists and wait. Carry it in a bucket, bowl or jug, or look at the barrel or pot that holds it.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-cheese\">cheese guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-kitchen-cottage": "Cottage Cheese",
	"quest-kitchen-cottage-desc": "Cottage cheese is eaten as it is or pressed into wheels.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Wrap curdled milk in linen and squeeze the whey out of it. Carry it in a bucket, bowl or jug, or look at the barrel or pot that holds it.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-cheese\">cheese guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-kitchen-wheels": "Cheese Wheels",
	"quest-kitchen-wheels-desc": "A raw cheese wheel is cottage cheese pressed with salt, ready to ripen.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Seal cottage cheese with salt in a barrel. Take out the raw wheel when it is done.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-cheese\">cheese guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-kitchen-cheddar": "Ripen Cheddar",
	"quest-kitchen-cheddar-desc": "Cheddar keeps for a very long time.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Put a raw cheese wheel on a shelf and leave it to ripen.<br><br><strong>Tip:</strong> A cool cellar slows spoiling while it ripens.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-cheese\">cheese guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-kitchen-blue": "Ripen Blue Cheese",
	"quest-kitchen-blue-desc": "Blue cheese needs the dark to ripen.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Put a raw blue cheese wheel on a shelf in a dark cellar and wait.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-cheese\">cheese guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-kitchen-waxed": "Waxed Cheddar",
	"quest-kitchen-waxed-desc": "A coat of wax makes cheddar last for years.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Combine a cheddar wheel with beeswax in the crafting grid.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-cheese\">cheese guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-kitchen-filled-0": "Have a fired crock",
	"quest-kitchen-filled": "Filled Crock",
	"quest-kitchen-filled-desc": "Meals keep much longer in a crock than in the pot.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Right-click a pot of cooked food with an empty crock to fill it. Have the filled crock on you.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://gamemechanicinfo-foodpreservation\">food preservation guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-kitchen-sealed": "Sealed Crock",
	"quest-kitchen-sealed-desc": "A sealed crock keeps a meal fresh for many months.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Put a filled crock in the crafting grid with fat or beeswax to seal it.<br><br><strong>Tip:</strong> Opening the crock to eat breaks the seal.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://gamemechanicinfo-foodpreservation\">food preservation guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-kitchen-jam": "Make Jam",
	"quest-kitchen-jam-desc": "Jam turns a berry harvest into food that lasts.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Cook two or more fruits with honey in a cooking pot. Take a serving in a bowl or a crock.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://gamemechanicinfo-foodpreservation\">food preservation guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-kitchen-shelf": "Shelf",
	"quest-kitchen-shelf-desc": "Shelves hold crocks, cheese wheels and small items.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Craft a shelf from boards in the crafting grid. Set it down in the world to finish the quest.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://gamemechanicinfo-foodpreservation\">food preservation guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-kitchen-cellar": "Build a Cellar",
	"quest-kitchen-cellar-desc": "Food spoils much slower in a cool, dark room.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Build a small closed room with no sky light, at most seven blocks wide, long and tall, with a solid door. Stand inside it.<br><br><strong>Tip:</strong> Walls of soil, stone or fired brick insulate best. Underground is coolest.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://gamemechanicinfo-foodpreservation\">food preservation guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-kitchen-stock-1": "Place a storage vessel, shelf or crock",
	"quest-kitchen-stock": "Stock the Cellar with Food",
	"quest-kitchen-stock-desc": "A stocked cellar carries you through the winter.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Stand in your cellar with a storage vessel, shelf or crock placed close by.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://gamemechanicinfo-foodpreservation\">food preservation guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-kitchen-salt": "Get Salt",
	"quest-kitchen-salt-desc": "Salt cures meat and makes brine and cheese.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Buy it from a trader, or mine halite, which is found in large domes under dry land.<br><br><strong>Tip:</strong> Halite is rare. Traders are often the faster way.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://gamemechanicinfo-foodpreservation\">food preservation guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-kitchen-cure-0": "Have any cured meat",
	"quest-kitchen-cure": "Cure Meat",
	"quest-kitchen-cure-desc": "Cured meat lasts for a year or more.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Seal raw meat with salt in a barrel and wait for it to cure.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://gamemechanicinfo-foodpreservation\">food preservation guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-kitchen-brine": "Make Brine",
	"quest-kitchen-brine-desc": "Brine is the liquid for pickling.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Mix water and salt in a barrel. Carry it in a bucket, bowl or jug, or look at the barrel or pot that holds it.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://gamemechanicinfo-foodpreservation\">food preservation guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-kitchen-pickle-0": "Have any pickled vegetable",
	"quest-kitchen-pickle": "Pickle Vegetables",
	"quest-kitchen-pickle-desc": "Pickled vegetables last through the longest winter.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Seal vegetables or legumes in a barrel of brine and wait.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://gamemechanicinfo-foodpreservation\">food preservation guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-kitchen-flour": "Grind Flour",
	"quest-kitchen-flour-desc": "Flour is the base of bread and pies.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Put grain in a quern and hold right-click to turn it.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-mealcooking\">meal cooking guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-kitchen-dough": "Make Dough",
	"quest-kitchen-dough-desc": "Dough is one step away from bread.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Combine flour with a bucket of water in the crafting grid.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-mealcooking\">meal cooking guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-kitchen-bread": "Bake Bread",
	"quest-kitchen-bread-desc": "Bread is filling and keeps well.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Bake dough in a clay oven. Heat the oven with firewood first, then put the dough in when the fire has burned out.<br><br><strong>Tip:</strong> Take it out once it is baked. Left too long it chars.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-mealcooking\">meal cooking guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-kitchen-pie-0": "Have a baked pie",
	"quest-kitchen-pie": "Bake a Pie",
	"quest-kitchen-pie-desc": "A pie holds four fillings and feeds like a full meal.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Place dough on a table, add fillings of fruit, meat or vegetables, close it with more dough, and bake it in a clay oven.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-mealcooking\">meal cooking guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-kitchen-press": "Build a Fruit Press",
	"quest-kitchen-press-desc": "The fruit press turns fruit into juice.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Craft the fruit press and its screw. The screw needs metal parts. Set it down in the world to finish the quest.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-alcohol\">alcohol guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-kitchen-juice-0": "Juice in a container you carry or look at",
	"quest-kitchen-juice": "Press Juice",
	"quest-kitchen-juice-desc": "Juice is a drink on its own and the start of cider and wine.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Put fruit in the press, set a bucket under it, and turn the screw. Carry it in a bucket, bowl or jug, or look at the barrel or pot that holds it.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-alcohol\">alcohol guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-kitchen-ferment-0": "Cider or wine in a container you carry or look at",
	"quest-kitchen-ferment": "Ferment a Drink",
	"quest-kitchen-ferment-desc": "Sealed juice turns to cider or wine.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Seal juice in a barrel for about a week. Carry it in a bucket, bowl or jug, or look at the barrel or pot that holds it.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-alcohol\">alcohol guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-kitchen-boiler-0": "Place a boiler",
	"quest-kitchen-boiler": "Build a Boiler",
	"quest-kitchen-boiler-desc": "A boiler is the heated half of a still.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Craft a boiler and place it on a firepit. Stand close to it so the quest can see it.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-alcohol\">alcohol guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-kitchen-distil-0": "A spirit in a container you carry or look at",
	"quest-kitchen-distil": "Distil Spirits",
	"quest-kitchen-distil-desc": "Spirits are made by boiling cider or wine.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Fill the boiler with a fermented drink, join a condenser to it with a bucket beneath, and light the fire. Carry it in a bucket, bowl or jug, or look at the barrel or pot that holds it.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-alcohol\">alcohol guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-kitchen-fed": "Well Fed",
	"quest-kitchen-fed-desc": "You have cooked, preserved, baked and brewed.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Finish the quests that lead here, then claim it.",
	"quest-kitchen-pan": "Form a Saucepan",
	"quest-kitchen-pan-desc": "The saucepan boils liquids on a fire pit and is the tool for broth, syrup and lard.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Clay form a saucepan and fire it in a pit kiln. Place it on a fire pit to boil what you put in its slots.<br><br>Part of the Expanded Foods mod.",
	"quest-kitchen-broth": "Simmer a Broth",
	"quest-kitchen-broth-desc": "Broth adds a rich base to stews, soups, pilaf and pasta.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Put a saucepan on a fire pit and boil water with bones, part-baked meat, fish or vegetables. Use one bone or piece for each litre of water. Carry it in a bucket, bowl or jug, or look at the barrel or pot that holds it.<br><br>Part of the Expanded Foods mod.",
	"quest-kitchen-lard": "Render Lard",
	"quest-kitchen-lard-desc": "Lard is cooking fat that keeps, and it stands in for food oil.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Boil a handful of fat with 0.2 litres of water in a saucepan.<br><br><strong>Tip:</strong> Lard hardens over time into rendered fat.<br><br>Part of the Expanded Foods mod.",
	"quest-kitchen-gratin": "Au Gratin",
	"quest-kitchen-gratin-desc": "Au gratin bakes vegetables and meat under cheese.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> In a cooking pot, cook 0.1 litres of milk or cottage cheese with a slice of cheese. Vegetables, meat, fish or sausage can go in the spare slots. Take a serving in a bowl.<br><br>Part of the Expanded Foods mod.",
	"quest-kitchen-saltwater": "Make Salt from Water",
	"quest-kitchen-saltwater-desc": "Sea water holds salt you can boil out.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Carry or look at a container of salt water, then simmer it in a saucepan until only salt is left. The handbook shows the exact recipe.<br><br>Part of the Expanded Foods mod.",
	"quest-kitchen-spile": "Make a Spile",
	"quest-kitchen-spile-desc": "A spile taps a tree for its sap.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Craft a spile as the handbook shows.<br><br><strong>Tip:</strong> Maple gives sap from January to March and birch from April to June.<br><br>Part of the Expanded Foods mod.",
	"quest-kitchen-tap": "Tap a Tree",
	"quest-kitchen-tap-desc": "Maple, birch and a few other trees give sap.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Push the spile into the trunk of a living maple or birch and place a bucket or saucepan under it. Stand close to it so the quest can see it.<br><br>Part of the Expanded Foods mod.",
	"quest-kitchen-tsyrup": "Boil Tree Syrup",
	"quest-kitchen-tsyrup-desc": "Sap boils down to sweet syrup.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Boil tree sap in a saucepan on a fire pit. Four parts sap make one part syrup. Carry it in a bucket, bowl or jug, or look at the barrel or pot that holds it.<br><br>Part of the Expanded Foods mod.",
	"objective-line-kitchen-resin-0": "Have resin",
	"quest-kitchen-resin": "Collect Resin",
	"quest-kitchen-resin-desc": "Tapped pines give fresh resin.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Put a spile in a pine tree between March and November, or an acacia between April and September, with a container under it. Let the resin harden, then tip it out.<br><br>Part of the Expanded Foods mod.",
	"quest-kitchen-bowl": "Make a Mixing Bowl",
	"quest-kitchen-bowl-desc": "The mixing bowl kneads ingredients into new foods and mixes meals.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Craft a mixing bowl as the handbook shows and place it. Put ingredients in its six top slots and hold right-click to knead.<br><br><strong>Tip:</strong> With a cooking pot in the lower left slot it mixes a meal instead.<br><br>Part of the Expanded Foods mod.",
	"objective-line-kitchen-egg-0": "Have an egg yolk or eggshell",
	"quest-kitchen-egg": "Crack an Egg",
	"quest-kitchen-egg-desc": "Yolk and white are used apart in many recipes.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Hold an egg over a bowl or bucket and crack it with Ctrl and right-click. You get egg white in the bowl and a yolk in your hand.<br><br><strong>Tip:</strong> Ctrl, Shift and right-click cracks the whole egg into liquid egg.<br><br>Part of the Expanded Foods mod.",
	"quest-kitchen-pasta": "Make Pasta",
	"quest-kitchen-pasta-desc": "Pasta is dough cut into noodles.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Knead a bag of flour with 0.1 litres of liquid egg in the mixing bowl. Flatten the dough with a hammer or rolling pin, then cut it into noodles with a knife.<br><br><strong>Tip:</strong> Baked noodles keep much longer.<br><br>Part of the Expanded Foods mod.",
	"quest-kitchen-hot": "Hot Pasta",
	"quest-kitchen-hot-desc": "Hot pasta is a filling cooked meal.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> In a cooking pot, cook one portion of noodles with one litre of water, vegetable juice or broth. Cheese, vegetables, meat or fish can go in the spare slots. Take a serving in a bowl.<br><br>Part of the Expanded Foods mod.",
	"quest-kitchen-cold": "Cold Pasta",
	"quest-kitchen-cold-desc": "Cold pasta is a meal for the road.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Boil noodles in a saucepan first. Put a cooking pot in the lower left slot of the mixing bowl, add the cooked noodles and any cheese, vegetables or cooked meat, and mix. Take a serving in a bowl.<br><br>Part of the Expanded Foods mod.",
	"quest-kitchen-nug": "Cut Meat into Nuggets",
	"quest-kitchen-nug-desc": "Small cuts cook faster and go into many recipes.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Hit raw meat with a stone or hammer to tenderise it, then slice it with a knife or cleaver into meat nuggets.<br><br>Part of the Expanded Foods mod.",
	"quest-kitchen-saus": "Make Sausages",
	"quest-kitchen-saus-desc": "Sausages keep longer than plain meat.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Knead a handful of fat or 0.1 litres of lard with a handful of meat nuggets in the mixing bowl.<br><br><strong>Tip:</strong> Add salt and the sausage cures while it hangs.<br><br>Part of the Expanded Foods mod.",
	"quest-kitchen-rack": "Build a Meat Rack",
	"quest-kitchen-rack-desc": "A meat rack lets meat hang and age.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Craft meat hooks and place them in a cool room. Stand close to it so the quest can see it.<br><br>Part of the Expanded Foods mod.",
	"quest-kitchen-hang": "Hang Meat to Age",
	"quest-kitchen-hang-desc": "Aged meat has more flavour and feeds you better.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Right-click the meat rack with raw meat or sausage and leave it to dry age. Cut the outside off the aged meat before you cook it.<br><br><strong>Tip:</strong> Meat that starts to rot before it has aged will not age.<br><br>Part of the Expanded Foods mod.",
	"quest-kitchen-dump": "Make Dumplings",
	"quest-kitchen-dump-desc": "Dumplings wrap a filling in dough.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Knead a handful of soft dough in the mixing bowl with meat nuggets, cheese or chopped vegetables. Cook or bake them.<br><br><strong>Tip:</strong> Dumplings go well in stews and soups.<br><br>Part of the Expanded Foods mod.",
	"quest-kitchen-salad": "Salad",
	"quest-kitchen-salad-desc": "Salad is a meal that needs no fire.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Put a cooking pot in the lower left slot of the mixing bowl, add two portions of chopped vegetables or soybeans, and mix. Take a serving in a bowl.<br><br>Part of the Expanded Foods mod.",
	"quest-kitchen-yogurt": "Make Yogurt",
	"quest-kitchen-yogurt-desc": "Yogurt keeps longer than milk.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Knead 0.1 litres of pasteurised milk with 0.1 litres of yogurt starter in the mixing bowl, then seal it in a barrel or bottle until it sets. Carry it in a bucket, bowl or jug, or look at the barrel or pot that holds it.<br><br>Part of the Expanded Foods mod.",
	"quest-kitchen-ymeal": "Yogurt Meal",
	"quest-kitchen-ymeal-desc": "Yogurt with fruit or nuts is a full meal.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Put a cooking pot in the lower left slot of the mixing bowl, add half a litre of yogurt and at least one fruit or handful of peanuts, and mix. Take a serving in a bowl.<br><br>Part of the Expanded Foods mod.",
	"quest-kitchen-starter": "Bread Starter",
	"quest-kitchen-starter-desc": "Bread starter makes better bread.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Seal dried berries in a barrel of water for four days, six handfuls to a litre. Mix the yeast water with a bag of flour and a handful of salt in the mixing bowl. Carry it in a bucket, bowl or jug, or look at the barrel or pot that holds it.<br><br>Part of the Expanded Foods mod.",
	"objective-line-kitchen-breaded-0": "Have any breaded food",
	"quest-kitchen-breaded": "Breaded Food",
	"quest-kitchen-breaded-desc": "A breadcrumb coat makes meat, fish and vegetables go further.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Knead a handful of bread crumbs, a bag of flour and 0.1 litres of liquid egg or oil with the food you want to coat. Cook, bake or fry it.<br><br>Part of the Expanded Foods mod.",
	"quest-kitchen-fruitbread": "Fruit Bread",
	"quest-kitchen-fruitbread-desc": "Fruit bread bakes fruit into the loaf.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Knead a ball of dough with fruit or nuts in the mixing bowl, then bake it in a clay oven.<br><br>Part of the Expanded Foods mod.",
	"quest-kitchen-bottle": "Make a Bottle",
	"quest-kitchen-bottle-desc": "Bottles carry drinks and sauces and can sit on a shelf or rack.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Clay form a bottle and fire it, or make one from glass.<br><br>Part of the Expanded Foods mod.",
	"quest-kitchen-vinegar": "Make Vinegar",
	"quest-kitchen-vinegar-desc": "Vinegar is used for pickling and sauces.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Seal wine or a spirit in a barrel and leave it for about two weeks. Carry it in a bucket, bowl or jug, or look at the barrel or pot that holds it.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-mealcooking\">meal cooking guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-kitchen-syrup": "Boil Fruit Syrup",
	"quest-kitchen-syrup-desc": "Fruit syrup sweetens other recipes.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Boil fruit juice in a saucepan on a fire pit. Four parts juice make one part syrup. Carry it in a bucket, bowl or jug, or look at the barrel or pot that holds it.<br><br>Part of the Expanded Foods mod.",
	"quest-kitchen-compote": "Compote",
	"quest-kitchen-compote-desc": "Compote is stewed fruit.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> In a cooking pot, cook 0.1 litres of syrup with a fruit. More fruit or peanuts can go in the spare slots. Take a serving in a bowl.<br><br>Part of the Expanded Foods mod.",
	"quest-kitchen-candy": "Make Candy",
	"quest-kitchen-candy-desc": "Candy is a small sweet that keeps well.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Knead 0.1 litres of honey, syrup or peanut butter with 0.1 litres of peanut paste or a handful of sunflower grain in the mixing bowl.<br><br>Part of the Expanded Foods mod.",
	"quest-kitchen-hardtack": "Hardtack",
	"quest-kitchen-hardtack-desc": "Hardtack is plain travel bread that lasts a very long time.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Knead a bag of flour, 0.1 litres of water and a handful of salt in the mixing bowl, then bake it.<br><br><strong>Tip:</strong> Bake it up to three more times and it lasts even longer.<br><br>Part of the Expanded Foods mod.",
	"quest-kitchen-gozinaki": "Gozinaki",
	"quest-kitchen-gozinaki-desc": "Gozinaki is a bar of nuts set in honey.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Knead a handful of peanuts or sunflower grain with a portion of honey in the mixing bowl, then bake it.<br><br>Part of the Expanded Foods mod.",
	"objective-line-kitchen-pemmican-0": "Have pemmican",
	"quest-kitchen-pemmican": "Pemmican",
	"quest-kitchen-pemmican-desc": "Pemmican packs meat, fat and berries into food for long trips.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Knead a handful of fat or 0.1 litres of lard with fruit and meat nuggets in the mixing bowl, then cook or bake it.<br><br><strong>Tip:</strong> Without Expanded Foods, follow the handbook's pemmican recipe.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-mealcooking\">meal cooking guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-kitchen-trailmix-0": "Have trail mix",
	"quest-kitchen-trailmix": "Trail Mix",
	"quest-kitchen-trailmix-desc": "Trail mix is a dry snack for the road.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Knead a handful of peanuts, a handful of soybeans or two cured meat nuggets, three handfuls of dried fruit and a slice of cheese in the mixing bowl.<br><br>Part of the Expanded Foods mod.",
	"objective-line-kitchen-sushi-0": "Have sushi",
	"quest-kitchen-sushi": "Sushi",
	"quest-kitchen-sushi-desc": "Sushi rolls rice with fish or vegetables.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Knead a sheet of dried seaweed with a handful of rice in the mixing bowl. Fish nuggets or chopped vegetables can be added.<br><br>Part of the Expanded Foods mod.",
	"quest-kitchen-pepper": "Stuffed Pepper",
	"quest-kitchen-pepper-desc": "A stuffed pepper is a small meal in itself.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Knead a bell pepper with a filling such as meat nuggets, chopped vegetables, grain or cheese in the mixing bowl, then cook or bake it.<br><br>Part of the Expanded Foods mod.",
	"quest-kitchen-muffin": "Muffins",
	"quest-kitchen-muffin-desc": "Muffins are small sweet breads.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Knead a ball of soft dough with fruit or nuts in the mixing bowl, then bake it.<br><br>Part of the Expanded Foods mod.",
	"objective-line-kitchen-softdough-0": "Have soft dough",
	"quest-kitchen-softdough": "Make Soft Dough",
	"quest-kitchen-softdough-desc": "Soft dough is the base for dumplings, muffins and pastry.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Knead a bag of flour with 0.1 litres of water or milk and 0.1 litres of liquid egg in the mixing bowl.<br><br>Part of the Expanded Foods mod.",
	"quest-kitchen-pasteur": "Pasteurize Milk",
	"quest-kitchen-pasteur-desc": "Heated milk keeps longer and is the start of yogurt.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Boil milk in a saucepan on a fire pit until it is pasteurised. Carry it in a bucket, bowl or jug, or look at the barrel or pot that holds it.<br><br>Part of the Expanded Foods mod.",
	"quest-kitchen-ystarter": "Yogurt Starter",
	"quest-kitchen-ystarter-desc": "A starter is what turns milk into yogurt.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Seal one litre of curdled milk with four handfuls of fresh fruit in a barrel for a day. Carry it in a bucket, bowl or jug, or look at the barrel or pot that holds it.<br><br>Part of the Expanded Foods mod.",
	"objective-line-kitchen-crystal-0": "Have a salt crystal",
	"quest-kitchen-crystal": "Crystallised Salt",
	"quest-kitchen-crystal-desc": "Salt grows as crystals from salt water.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Seal ten litres of salt water or five litres of brine in a barrel to grow a damp salt crystal, or boil the same amount for a dry one.<br><br>Part of the Expanded Foods mod.",
	"quest-kitchen-drysalt": "Dry Salt Crystal",
	"quest-kitchen-drysalt-desc": "A damp salt crystal has to dry before use.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Leave a damp salt crystal to dry out. Grind the dry crystal in a quern to get salt.<br><br>Part of the Expanded Foods mod.",
	"quest-kitchen-fermfish": "Ferment Fish",
	"quest-kitchen-fermfish-desc": "Fermented fish is the start of fish sauce.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Seal raw fish with salt in a barrel for two weeks. Use eight salt for every 64 fish. Carry it in a bucket, bowl or jug, or look at the barrel or pot that holds it.<br><br>Part of the Expanded Foods mod.",
	"quest-kitchen-fishsauce": "Press Fish Sauce",
	"quest-kitchen-fishsauce-desc": "Fish sauce seasons many meals.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Press the fermented fish in the fruit press with a bucket under it. Carry it in a bucket, bowl or jug, or look at the barrel or pot that holds it.<br><br>Part of the Expanded Foods mod.",
	"quest-kitchen-agewine": "Age Wine",
	"quest-kitchen-agewine-desc": "Wine grows stronger with age.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Seal wine in a barrel or keep it in bottles and leave it to cure. Carry it in a bucket, bowl or jug, or look at the barrel or pot that holds it.<br><br>Part of the Expanded Foods mod.",
	"quest-kitchen-finewine": "Make Fine Wine",
	"quest-kitchen-finewine-desc": "Fine wine is wine aged a second time.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Seal strong wine again and leave it to cure once more. Carry it in a bucket, bowl or jug, or look at the barrel or pot that holds it.<br><br>Part of the Expanded Foods mod.",
	"quest-kitchen-agespirit": "Age a Spirit",
	"quest-kitchen-agespirit-desc": "Spirits also improve with age.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Seal a spirit in a barrel or keep it in bottles and leave it to cure. Carry it in a bucket, bowl or jug, or look at the barrel or pot that holds it.<br><br>Part of the Expanded Foods mod.",
	"quest-kitchen-aqua": "Distil Aqua Vitae",
	"quest-kitchen-aqua-desc": "Aqua vitae is the strongest spirit.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Age a strong spirit once more in a sealed barrel or bottle. Carry it in a bucket, bowl or jug, or look at the barrel or pot that holds it.<br><br>Part of the Expanded Foods mod.",
	"objective-line-kitchen-brack-0": "Place a bottle rack",
	"quest-kitchen-brack": "Build a Bottle Rack",
	"quest-kitchen-brack-desc": "A bottle rack stores bottles neatly in the cellar.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Craft a bottle rack as the handbook shows and place it. Set it down in the world to finish the quest.<br><br>Part of the Expanded Foods mod.",
	"objective-line-kitchen-condenser-0": "Place a condenser",
	"quest-kitchen-condenser": "Build a Condenser",
	"quest-kitchen-condenser-desc": "The condenser cools the vapour from the boiler back into a drink.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Craft a condenser and place it beside the boiler with a bucket under its spout. Stand close to it so the quest can see it.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-alcohol\">alcohol guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-kitchen-crumbs": "Make Breadcrumbs",
	"quest-kitchen-crumbs-desc": "Bread crumbs use up old bread.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Tear a loaf of bread apart in the crafting grid, or grind it in a quern.<br><br>Part of the Expanded Foods mod.",
	"quest-kitchen-feed": "Crumb Feed",
	"quest-kitchen-feed-desc": "Crumb feed is animal feed made from bread crumbs.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Put bread crumbs in the crafting grid to make bread crumb feed.<br><br>Part of the Expanded Foods mod.",
	"quest-kitchen-roast": "Roast Grain",
	"quest-kitchen-roast-desc": "Roasted grain is a snack and an ingredient.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Cook grain in the top slot of a fire pit.<br><br>Part of the Expanded Foods mod.",
	"objective-line-kitchen-pilaf-0": "Carry a cooked pilaf",
	"quest-kitchen-pilaf": "Pilaf",
	"quest-kitchen-pilaf-desc": "Pilaf is rice cooked in stock.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Put a cooking pot on a fire pit and cook one slot of rice with one slot of stock or broth. Vegetables can go in the spare slots. Take a serving in a bowl. The handbook shows the exact recipe.<br><br>Part of the Expanded Foods mod.",
	"chapter-kitchen": "Kitchen Cooking",
	"quest-farm-hoe": "Make a Hoe",
	"quest-farm-hoe-desc": "A hoe turns soil into farmland.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Knap a hoe head from flint or stone and put it on a stick in the crafting grid.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://gamemechanicinfo-farming\">farming guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-farm-farmland": "Make Farmland",
	"quest-farm-farmland-desc": "Crops only grow on tilled soil.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Right-click soil with the hoe to till it. Stand beside your farmland.<br><br><strong>Tip:</strong> Darker soil is more fertile and grows crops faster.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://gamemechanicinfo-farming\">farming guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-farm-seeds": "Gather Seeds",
	"quest-farm-seeds-desc": "Wild crops are where every farm begins.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Break wild crops you find while exploring to get their seeds. Carry four seeds.<br><br><strong>Tip:</strong> A knife or scythe gives seeds more often than bare hands.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://gamemechanicinfo-farming\">farming guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-farm-plant": "Plant Your First Crops",
	"quest-farm-plant-desc": "Each crop wants its own season and climate.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Right-click farmland with seeds to sow them. Stand beside your growing crops.<br><br><strong>Tip:</strong> Hold a seed and read its tooltip to see which temperatures it can stand.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://gamemechanicinfo-farming\">farming guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-farm-harvest-0": "Have any grain, vegetable or legume",
	"quest-farm-harvest": "Collect the First Harvest",
	"quest-farm-harvest-desc": "A ripe crop gives food and fresh seeds.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Wait until the crop is fully grown, then break it. Carry any grain, vegetable or legume.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://gamemechanicinfo-farming\">farming guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-farm-ggrain-0": "Have a hoe",
	"objective-line-farm-ggrain-1": "Stand at your farmland",
	"quest-farm-ggrain": "Grow Grains",
	"quest-farm-ggrain-desc": "Grains feed you as porridge and bread, and they feed your animals.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Finish the quests that lead here. Then stand at your farmland with a hoe.",
	"objective-line-farm-gveg-0": "Have a hoe",
	"objective-line-farm-gveg-1": "Stand at your farmland",
	"quest-farm-gveg": "Grow Vegetables",
	"quest-farm-gveg-desc": "Vegetables make soups, stews and pickles.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Finish the quests that lead here. Then stand at your farmland with a hoe.",
	"quest-farm-g0": "Grow Spelt",
	"quest-farm-g0-desc": "Spelt is the hardy grain of mild lands.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Find wild spelt for seeds, sow it on farmland in the right season, and harvest it when ripe. Carry eight.<br><br><strong>Tip:</strong> The seed's tooltip shows the temperatures it can stand.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://gamemechanicinfo-farming\">farming guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-farm-g1": "Grow Rye",
	"quest-farm-g1-desc": "Rye stands the cold better than any other grain.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Find wild rye for seeds, sow it on farmland in the right season, and harvest it when ripe. Carry eight.<br><br><strong>Tip:</strong> The seed's tooltip shows the temperatures it can stand.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://gamemechanicinfo-farming\">farming guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-farm-g2": "Grow Flax",
	"quest-farm-g2-desc": "Flax gives grain to eat and fibres for twine and linen.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Find wild flax for seeds, sow it on farmland in the right season, and harvest it when ripe. Carry eight.<br><br><strong>Tip:</strong> The seed's tooltip shows the temperatures it can stand.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://gamemechanicinfo-farming\">farming guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-farm-g3": "Grow Rice",
	"quest-farm-g3-desc": "Rice likes heat and gives a heavy harvest.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Find wild rice for seeds, sow it on farmland in the right season, and harvest it when ripe. Carry eight.<br><br><strong>Tip:</strong> The seed's tooltip shows the temperatures it can stand.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://gamemechanicinfo-farming\">farming guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-farm-g4": "Grow Amaranth",
	"quest-farm-g4-desc": "Amaranth is a warm climate grain.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Find wild amaranth for seeds, sow it on farmland in the right season, and harvest it when ripe. Carry eight.<br><br><strong>Tip:</strong> The seed's tooltip shows the temperatures it can stand.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://gamemechanicinfo-farming\">farming guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-farm-g5": "Grow Sunflower",
	"quest-farm-g5-desc": "Sunflowers like warmth and give oily seeds.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Find wild sunflower for seeds, sow it on farmland in the right season, and harvest it when ripe. Carry eight.<br><br><strong>Tip:</strong> The seed's tooltip shows the temperatures it can stand.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://gamemechanicinfo-farming\">farming guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-farm-g6-0": "Have 8 × cassava",
	"quest-farm-g6": "Grow Cassava",
	"quest-farm-g6-desc": "Cassava grows only in hot lands.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Find wild cassava for seeds, sow it on farmland in the right season, and harvest it when ripe. Carry eight.<br><br><strong>Tip:</strong> The seed's tooltip shows the temperatures it can stand.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://gamemechanicinfo-farming\">farming guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-farm-v0": "Grow Carrots",
	"quest-farm-v0-desc": "Carrots grow quickly in mild weather.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Find wild carrots for seeds, sow them on farmland in the right season, and harvest when ripe. Carry eight.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://gamemechanicinfo-farming\">farming guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-farm-v1": "Grow Onions",
	"quest-farm-v1-desc": "Onions keep well in a storage vessel.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Find wild onions for seeds, sow them on farmland in the right season, and harvest when ripe. Carry eight.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://gamemechanicinfo-farming\">farming guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-farm-v2": "Grow Turnips",
	"quest-farm-v2-desc": "Turnips are fast and stand some cold.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Find wild turnips for seeds, sow them on farmland in the right season, and harvest when ripe. Carry eight.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://gamemechanicinfo-farming\">farming guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-farm-v3": "Grow Parsnips",
	"quest-farm-v3-desc": "Parsnips are a hardy root for cool lands.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Find wild parsnips for seeds, sow them on farmland in the right season, and harvest when ripe. Carry eight.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://gamemechanicinfo-farming\">farming guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-farm-v4": "Grow Cabbage",
	"quest-farm-v4-desc": "Cabbage is slow but gives a lot of food.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Find wild cabbage for seeds, sow them on farmland in the right season, and harvest when ripe. Carry eight.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://gamemechanicinfo-farming\">farming guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-farm-v5": "Grow Pumpkins",
	"quest-farm-v5-desc": "Pumpkin vines spread, so leave empty farmland beside them.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Find wild pumpkins for seeds, sow them on farmland in the right season, and harvest when ripe. Carry four.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://gamemechanicinfo-farming\">farming guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-farm-v6": "Grow Bell Peppers",
	"quest-farm-v6-desc": "Bell peppers need a warm climate.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Find wild bell peppers for seeds, sow them on farmland in the right season, and harvest when ripe. Carry eight.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://gamemechanicinfo-farming\">farming guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-farm-bring": "Bring in the Harvest",
	"quest-farm-bring-desc": "A full harvest sees the whole colony through winter.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Carry 64 of any grains and 32 of any vegetables.<br><br><strong>Tip:</strong> They can be mixed kinds. Split them over several stacks if you need to.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://gamemechanicinfo-farming\">farming guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-farm-compost": "Make Compost",
	"quest-farm-compost-desc": "Rotten food is not wasted. It becomes compost.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Seal rot in a barrel and wait for it to turn into compost.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://gamemechanicinfo-farming\">farming guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-farm-soy": "Grow Soybeans",
	"quest-farm-soy-desc": "Soybeans are a legume and put nitrogen back in the soil.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Grow soybeans on farmland and carry eight.<br><br>Part of the Expanded Foods mod.",
	"quest-farm-soak": "Soak Soybeans",
	"quest-farm-soak-desc": "Soaking is the first step of working soybeans.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Seal soybeans in a barrel of water, one litre for each portion, and wait three days.<br><br>Part of the Expanded Foods mod.",
	"quest-farm-grind": "Grind Roasted Soybeans",
	"quest-farm-grind-desc": "Roasted soybeans grind to a powder for soy sauce.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Roast soaked soybeans over a fire pit or in an oven, then grind them in a quern.<br><br>Part of the Expanded Foods mod.",
	"quest-farm-soymilk": "Make Soy Milk",
	"quest-farm-soymilk-desc": "Soy milk stands in for milk where you have no animals.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Shell soaked soybeans in the crafting grid, mix them with a litre of water, grind the mix in a quern, press it in the fruit press and boil the raw soy milk. Carry it in a bucket, bowl or jug, or look at the barrel or pot that holds it.<br><br>Part of the Expanded Foods mod.",
	"quest-farm-culture": "Culture Soybeans",
	"quest-farm-culture-desc": "Cultured soybeans are the start of soy sauce.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Knead roasted soybean powder with any grain in the mixing bowl or crafting grid.<br><br>Part of the Expanded Foods mod.",
	"quest-farm-brew": "Brew Soy Sauce",
	"quest-farm-brew-desc": "Soy sauce seasons many meals.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Soak cultured soybeans in a litre of brine in a sealed barrel for a week, then press the slurry in the fruit press. Carry it in a bucket, bowl or jug, or look at the barrel or pot that holds it.<br><br>Part of the Expanded Foods mod.",
	"quest-farm-quern": "Make a Quern",
	"quest-farm-quern-desc": "A quern grinds grain to flour and bones to bone meal.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Craft a quern from hard stone such as granite, andesite or basalt. Set it down in the world to finish the quest.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://gamemechanicinfo-farming\">farming guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-farm-water": "Water Your Crops",
	"quest-farm-water-desc": "Moist soil grows crops faster.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Fill a fired watering can at any water, then hold right-click over your farmland until it is at least three quarters moist. Stand beside the field with the can on you.<br><br><strong>Tip:</strong> Farmland within three blocks of water stays moist by itself.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://gamemechanicinfo-farming\">farming guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-farm-fence": "Fence Your Field",
	"quest-farm-fence-desc": "Hares and other animals eat unguarded crops.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Craft wooden fences and put them all the way round your field. Set it down in the world to finish the quest.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://gamemechanicinfo-farming\">farming guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-farm-richsoil-0": "Have rich soil or terra preta",
	"quest-farm-richsoil": "Find Rich Soil",
	"quest-farm-richsoil-desc": "Rich soil grows every crop faster.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Dig up high fertility soil where you find it in lush forests, or make terra preta, the best soil of all. Carry a block of it.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://gamemechanicinfo-farming\">farming guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-farm-scythe": "Make a Scythe",
	"quest-farm-scythe-desc": "A scythe cuts a wide swathe of crops or grass in one swing.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Smith a scythe blade on an anvil and put it on a stick.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://gamemechanicinfo-farming\">farming guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-farm-peanut": "Grow Peanuts",
	"quest-farm-peanut-desc": "Peanuts are a legume that likes warmth.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Grow peanuts on farmland and carry eight.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://gamemechanicinfo-farming\">farming guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-farm-roastp": "Roast Peanuts",
	"quest-farm-roastp-desc": "Roasted peanuts are a snack and an ingredient.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Cook peanuts in the top slot of a fire pit.<br><br>Part of the Expanded Foods mod.",
	"quest-farm-paste": "Peanut Paste",
	"quest-farm-paste-desc": "Peanut paste is ground peanut kernels.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Break peanuts apart in the crafting grid to get the kernels, then grind the kernels in a quern. Carry it in a bucket, bowl or jug, or look at the barrel or pot that holds it.<br><br>Part of the Expanded Foods mod.",
	"quest-farm-butter": "Peanut Butter",
	"quest-farm-butter-desc": "Peanut butter keeps well and fills you up.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Knead equal parts of peanut paste and food oil in the mixing bowl. Honey and salt can be added. Carry it in a bucket, bowl or jug, or look at the barrel or pot that holds it.<br><br>Part of the Expanded Foods mod.",
	"quest-farm-pineapple": "Grow Pineapple",
	"quest-farm-pineapple-desc": "Pineapples grow only in hot places.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Find or grow a pineapple plant in a warm climate and pick the fruit.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://gamemechanicinfo-farming\">farming guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-farm-bone": "Grind Bone Meal",
	"quest-farm-bone-desc": "Bone meal feeds the soil with phosphorus.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Grind bones in a quern.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://gamemechanicinfo-farming\">farming guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-farm-potash": "Get Potash",
	"quest-farm-potash-desc": "Potash feeds the soil with potassium.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> The handbook lists where potash comes from. Carry some.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://gamemechanicinfo-farming\">farming guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-farm-fert": "Fertilise a Field",
	"quest-farm-fert-desc": "Crops use up the soil. Fertiliser puts it back.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Hold bone meal, potash, saltpeter or compost and right-click your farmland with it.<br><br><strong>Tip:</strong> Look at farmland to see its three nutrients, N, P and K.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://gamemechanicinfo-farming\">farming guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-farm-rotate": "Rotate Your Crops",
	"quest-farm-rotate-desc": "Each crop drains a different nutrient, so mixing and swapping crops rests the soil.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Sow a different kind of crop after each harvest. Stand beside a field with at least twelve crops growing, of two kinds or more.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://gamemechanicinfo-farming\">farming guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-farm-green": "Build a Greenhouse",
	"quest-farm-green-desc": "A greenhouse lets crops grow in the cold.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Build a closed room where most of the roof is glass. Stand inside it.<br><br><strong>Tip:</strong> A greenhouse is about five degrees warmer than outside.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://gamemechanicinfo-greenhouse\">greenhouse guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-farm-master": "Master Farmer",
	"quest-farm-master-desc": "You have grown, harvested, fertilised and kept bees.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Finish the quests that lead here, then claim it.",
	"quest-farm-oil": "Press Food Oil",
	"quest-farm-oil-desc": "Food oil is pressed from oily seeds.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Put flax grain, rice, seeds, soybeans or olives in the fruit press with a bucket under it and press. Carry it in a bucket, bowl or jug, or look at the barrel or pot that holds it.<br><br>Part of the Expanded Foods mod.",
	"quest-farm-cutting": "Take a Bush Cutting",
	"quest-farm-cutting-desc": "A cutting grows into a new bush where you want it.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Use shears or a knife on a wild berry bush to take a cutting.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://gamemechanicinfo-farming\">farming guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-farm-bush-0": "Plant a berry bush",
	"quest-farm-bush": "Plant a Bush",
	"quest-farm-bush-desc": "Bushes near home mean berries without the walk.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Plant a cutting or a dug-up bush in soil. Stand beside it.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://gamemechanicinfo-farming\">farming guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-farm-tcutting-0": "Have a fruit tree cutting",
	"quest-farm-tcutting": "Take a Fruit Tree Cutting",
	"quest-farm-tcutting-desc": "Fruit trees are grown from cuttings, not seeds.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Use shears on the leafy end of a fruit tree branch to take a cutting.<br><br><strong>Tip:</strong> Only take a few from each tree so it keeps growing.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://gamemechanicinfo-fruittrees\">fruit trees guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-farm-tree": "Plant a Fruit Tree",
	"quest-farm-tree-desc": "A fruit tree takes a year or more to bear fruit.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Plant a fruit tree cutting in soil. Stand beside it.<br><br><strong>Tip:</strong> Not every cutting takes root. Plant a few.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://gamemechanicinfo-fruittrees\">fruit trees guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-farm-shears": "Make Shears",
	"quest-farm-shears-desc": "Shears take cuttings and collect leaves and vines.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Smith shear blades on an anvil and craft them into shears.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://gamemechanicinfo-farming\">farming guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-farm-pickb-0": "Have any berries",
	"quest-farm-pickb": "Pick Your First Berries",
	"quest-farm-pickb-desc": "Berries ripen through the warm months.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Right-click a ripe berry bush to pick it.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://gamemechanicinfo-farming\">farming guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-farm-graft": "Graft a Cutting",
	"quest-farm-graft-desc": "Grafting puts a second kind of fruit on one tree.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Hold a fruit tree cutting and right-click the cut end of a branch on another fruit tree. Stand beside the tree with a knife on you.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://gamemechanicinfo-fruittrees\">fruit trees guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-farm-pickf-0": "Have any tree fruit",
	"quest-farm-pickf": "Pick Your First Fruit",
	"quest-farm-pickf-desc": "Each fruit tree ripens once a year.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Right-click ripe fruit on the tree to pick it. Carry any tree fruit.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://gamemechanicinfo-fruittrees\">fruit trees guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-farm-orchard": "Plant an Orchard",
	"quest-farm-orchard-desc": "Several trees give fruit through more of the year.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Plant four fruit trees close together and stand among them.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://gamemechanicinfo-fruittrees\">fruit trees guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-farm-store": "Store Your Seeds",
	"quest-farm-store-desc": "Seeds kept safe are next year's harvest.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Put seeds in a storage vessel or chest. Look at the container with the seeds inside.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://gamemechanicinfo-farming\">farming guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-farm-dry": "Dry Fruit",
	"quest-farm-dry-desc": "Dried fruit keeps for a long time.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Bake fruit in a clay oven to dry it.<br><br>Part of the Expanded Foods mod.",
	"quest-farm-leather": "Fruit Leather",
	"quest-farm-leather-desc": "Fruit leather is fruit pulp dried flat.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> After pressing juice, simmer the leftover mash in a saucepan with 0.1 litres of water and 0.2 litres of honey or syrup.<br><br>Part of the Expanded Foods mod.",
	"quest-farm-candied": "Candied Fruit",
	"quest-farm-candied-desc": "Candied fruit is fruit kept in sugar.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Boil a fresh fruit with 0.1 litres of syrup of the same fruit in a saucepan.<br><br>Part of the Expanded Foods mod.",
	"objective-line-farm-bars-0": "Have a fruit bar",
	"quest-farm-bars": "Fruit Bars",
	"quest-farm-bars-desc": "Fruit bars are a travel food.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Knead a handful of peanuts or sunflower grain, a fruit, a gelatin and 0.1 litres of honey or syrup in the mixing bowl.<br><br>Part of the Expanded Foods mod.",
	"quest-farm-b0": "Blueberries",
	"quest-farm-b0-desc": "Blueberries grow on bushes in the wild.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Pick ripe blueberries from bushes and carry eight.<br><br><strong>Tip:</strong> A bush fruits again after a while, so remember where it is.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://gamemechanicinfo-farming\">farming guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-farm-b1": "Cranberries",
	"quest-farm-b1-desc": "Cranberries grow on bushes in the wild.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Pick ripe cranberries from bushes and carry eight.<br><br><strong>Tip:</strong> A bush fruits again after a while, so remember where it is.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://gamemechanicinfo-farming\">farming guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-farm-b2": "Redcurrants",
	"quest-farm-b2-desc": "Redcurrants grow on bushes in the wild.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Pick ripe redcurrants from bushes and carry eight.<br><br><strong>Tip:</strong> A bush fruits again after a while, so remember where it is.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://gamemechanicinfo-farming\">farming guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-farm-b3": "Blackcurrants",
	"quest-farm-b3-desc": "Blackcurrants grow on bushes in the wild.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Pick ripe blackcurrants from bushes and carry eight.<br><br><strong>Tip:</strong> A bush fruits again after a while, so remember where it is.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://gamemechanicinfo-farming\">farming guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-farm-b4": "Whitecurrants",
	"quest-farm-b4-desc": "Whitecurrants grow on bushes in the wild.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Pick ripe whitecurrants from bushes and carry eight.<br><br><strong>Tip:</strong> A bush fruits again after a while, so remember where it is.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://gamemechanicinfo-farming\">farming guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-farm-f0-0": "Have an apple",
	"quest-farm-f0": "Apples",
	"quest-farm-f0-desc": "Apple trees grow in mild climates.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Find a wild tree or grow one from a cutting, and pick the ripe apples.<br><br><strong>Tip:</strong> Fruit trees flower in spring and ripen later in the year.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://gamemechanicinfo-fruittrees\">fruit trees guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-farm-f1": "Cherries",
	"quest-farm-f1-desc": "Cherry trees grow in mild climates.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Find a wild tree or grow one from a cutting, and pick the ripe cherries.<br><br><strong>Tip:</strong> Fruit trees flower in spring and ripen later in the year.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://gamemechanicinfo-fruittrees\">fruit trees guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-farm-f2": "Peaches",
	"quest-farm-f2-desc": "Peach trees like warm summers.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Find a wild tree or grow one from a cutting, and pick the ripe peaches.<br><br><strong>Tip:</strong> Fruit trees flower in spring and ripen later in the year.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://gamemechanicinfo-fruittrees\">fruit trees guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-farm-f3": "Pears",
	"quest-farm-f3-desc": "Pear trees grow in mild climates.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Find a wild tree or grow one from a cutting, and pick the ripe pears.<br><br><strong>Tip:</strong> Fruit trees flower in spring and ripen later in the year.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://gamemechanicinfo-fruittrees\">fruit trees guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-farm-f4": "Oranges",
	"quest-farm-f4-desc": "Orange trees need a warm climate.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Find a wild tree or grow one from a cutting, and pick the ripe oranges.<br><br><strong>Tip:</strong> Fruit trees flower in spring and ripen later in the year.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://gamemechanicinfo-fruittrees\">fruit trees guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-farm-f5": "Mangoes",
	"quest-farm-f5-desc": "Mango trees grow only in hot lands.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Find a wild tree or grow one from a cutting, and pick the ripe mangoes.<br><br><strong>Tip:</strong> Fruit trees flower in spring and ripen later in the year.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://gamemechanicinfo-fruittrees\">fruit trees guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-farm-f6": "Breadfruit",
	"quest-farm-f6-desc": "Breadfruit trees grow only in hot lands.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Find a wild tree or grow one from a cutting, and pick the ripe breadfruit.<br><br><strong>Tip:</strong> Fruit trees flower in spring and ripen later in the year.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://gamemechanicinfo-fruittrees\">fruit trees guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-farm-f7": "Lychees",
	"quest-farm-f7-desc": "Lychee trees need a warm, wet climate.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Find a wild tree or grow one from a cutting, and pick the ripe lychees.<br><br><strong>Tip:</strong> Fruit trees flower in spring and ripen later in the year.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://gamemechanicinfo-fruittrees\">fruit trees guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-farm-f8": "Pomegranates",
	"quest-farm-f8-desc": "Pomegranate trees like warm, dry lands.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Find a wild tree or grow one from a cutting, and pick the ripe pomegranates.<br><br><strong>Tip:</strong> Fruit trees flower in spring and ripen later in the year.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://gamemechanicinfo-fruittrees\">fruit trees guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-farm-skep": "Make a Skep",
	"quest-farm-skep-desc": "A skep is a woven basket hive.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Craft a skep from cattails or papyrus in the crafting grid. Set it down in the world to finish the quest.",
	"objective-line-farm-colony-0": "A skep with bees in it near you",
	"quest-farm-colony": "Move a Colony",
	"quest-farm-colony-desc": "Wild bees move into an empty skep by themselves.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Place an empty skep within a few blocks of a wild hive, with flowers nearby, and wait for a swarm. Stand beside the skep once bees live in it.<br><br><strong>Tip:</strong> More flowers close by makes the bees swarm sooner.",
	"quest-farm-comb": "Harvest Honeycomb",
	"quest-farm-comb-desc": "A full skep is harvested by breaking it.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Wait until the skep is ready to harvest, then break it.<br><br><strong>Tip:</strong> Put a new empty skep nearby first so you do not lose your bees.",
	"quest-farm-wax": "Collect Beeswax",
	"quest-farm-wax-desc": "Beeswax seals crocks and coats cheese.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Squeeze honeycomb over a bucket. The wax stays in your hands.",
	"quest-farm-honey": "Squeeze Out Honey",
	"quest-farm-honey-desc": "Honey sweetens meals and never spoils.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Hold honeycomb and right-click a bucket to squeeze the honey into it. Carry it in a bucket, bowl or jug, or look at the barrel or pot that holds it.",
	"quest-farm-cer": "Form a Ceramic Hive",
	"quest-farm-cer-desc": "A ceramic hive can be harvested again and again without losing the bees.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Form a ceramic brood pot and a honey pot from clay and fire both.<br><br>Part of the From Golden Combs mod.",
	"quest-farm-cermove": "Move Bees into the Hive",
	"quest-farm-cermove-desc": "A ceramic hive is filled from a skep.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Place the brood pot and move bees into it from a skep that has bees in it. Stand beside the hive.<br><br>Part of the From Golden Combs mod.",
	"quest-farm-cerharv": "Harvest the Honey Pot",
	"quest-farm-cerharv-desc": "The honey pot on top fills with comb.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> When the honey pot is full, scrape it with a knife. Stand beside the hive with honeycomb on you.<br><br>Part of the From Golden Combs mod.",
	"objective-line-farm-pollin-0": "A ceramic or Langstroth hive near you",
	"quest-farm-pollin": "Bees Among the Crops",
	"quest-farm-pollin-desc": "Hives near a field make the crops give more.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Place a ceramic or Langstroth hive close to your crops and stand beside both.<br><br><strong>Tip:</strong> A skep adds about a tenth, a ceramic hive a fifth and a Langstroth hive almost a third.<br><br>Part of the From Golden Combs mod.",
	"objective-line-farm-panels-0": "Have a hive panel",
	"quest-farm-panels": "Make Hive Panels",
	"quest-farm-panels-desc": "A Langstroth hive is built from wooden panels.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Craft the hive panels from boards.<br><br>Part of the From Golden Combs mod.",
	"quest-farm-rack": "Build a Frame Rack",
	"quest-farm-rack-desc": "The frame rack is the workbench for bee frames.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Craft a frame rack. Set it down in the world to finish the quest.<br><br>Part of the From Golden Combs mod.",
	"quest-farm-frames": "Line Bee Frames",
	"quest-farm-frames-desc": "Bees build their comb on lined frames.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Craft bee frames and a frame liner, then line the frames in the frame rack.<br><br>Part of the From Golden Combs mod.",
	"objective-line-farm-lang-0": "Place a Langstroth hive",
	"quest-farm-lang": "Build a Langstroth Hive",
	"quest-farm-lang-desc": "The Langstroth hive is the best hive there is.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Place the base, add a brood box and up to three supers, and fill each super with ten lined frames. Stand beside it.<br><br>Part of the From Golden Combs mod.",
	"quest-farm-harvf": "Harvest a Frame",
	"quest-farm-harvf-desc": "Frames are harvested one at a time and the bees stay.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Take a full frame from a super and harvest it in the frame rack.<br><br>Part of the From Golden Combs mod.",
	"quest-farm-twine": "Repair a Frame",
	"quest-farm-twine-desc": "Frames wear out with each harvest.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Craft waxed flax twine and use it in the frame rack to repair a frame.<br><br>Part of the From Golden Combs mod.",
	"chapter-farming": "Farming",
	"quest-carp-sapling": "Plant a Sapling",
	"quest-carp-sapling-desc": "Trees you plant are wood you never have to walk for.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Break leaves until a sapling drops, or pick one up after felling a tree. Set it down in the world to finish the quest.",
	"quest-carp-grow": "Grow a Tree",
	"quest-carp-grow-desc": "A sapling needs open sky and room above it.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Plant a sapling on soil and wait for it to grow into a tree. Only a sapling you planted yourself counts.<br><br><strong>Tip:</strong> Different trees grow at very different speeds.",
	"objective-line-carp-fell-0": "Chop 12 logs from grown trees with an axe",
	"quest-carp-fell": "Fell a Great Tree",
	"quest-carp-fell-desc": "Chop the lowest log and the whole tree comes down.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Cut down grown trees with an axe until you have broken twelve logs.<br><br><strong>Tip:</strong> Bigger trees take longer to chop but give far more wood.",
	"quest-carp-resin": "Collect Resin",
	"quest-carp-resin-desc": "Resin is a glue and a fuel for torches and lanterns.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Look for pine trunks with a yellow leak on the bark and right-click to collect it.<br><br><strong>Tip:</strong> Leave the log standing. The resin grows back.",
	"quest-carp-saw": "Make a Saw",
	"quest-carp-saw-desc": "A saw is what turns logs into boards.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Smith a saw blade on an anvil and put it on a stick.",
	"quest-carp-boards": "Saw Boards",
	"quest-carp-boards-desc": "Boards are the stuff of every piece of furniture.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Put a saw and a log in the crafting grid. Carry sixteen boards.",
	"quest-carp-bucket": "Make a Bucket",
	"quest-carp-bucket-desc": "A bucket carries water, milk and other liquids.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Craft a wooden bucket from boards.",
	"quest-carp-barrel": "Make a Barrel",
	"quest-carp-barrel-desc": "Barrels hold liquids and are where food is pickled, cured, tanned and brewed.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Craft a barrel from boards. Set it down in the world to finish the quest.",
	"quest-carp-chest": "Build a Chest",
	"quest-carp-chest-desc": "A chest is your first real storage.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Craft a chest from boards and nails. Set it down in the world to finish the quest.",
	"quest-carp-trunk": "Build a Trunk",
	"quest-carp-trunk-desc": "A trunk holds twice what a chest does.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Craft a trunk from boards and nails. Set it down in the world to finish the quest.",
	"quest-carp-door": "Make a Door",
	"quest-carp-door-desc": "A door keeps the weather and the wolves out.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Craft a door from boards. Set it down in the world to finish the quest.",
	"quest-carp-trapdoor": "Make a Trapdoor",
	"quest-carp-trapdoor-desc": "A trapdoor closes off a cellar or a shaft.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Craft a trapdoor from boards. Set it down in the world to finish the quest.",
	"quest-carp-ladder": "Make a Ladder",
	"quest-carp-ladder-desc": "Ladders get you up walls and down mines.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Craft a ladder from sticks and boards. Set it down in the world to finish the quest.",
	"quest-carp-fence": "Build a Fence and Gate",
	"quest-carp-fence-desc": "Fences pen animals and guard crops.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Craft wooden fences from sticks and a gate to get in and out. Place a fence and a gate. Set it down in the world to finish the quest.",
	"quest-carp-stairs": "Plank Stairs and Slabs",
	"quest-carp-stairs-desc": "Stairs and slabs shape roofs and floors.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Craft plank stairs and plank slabs from planks and place one of each. Set it down in the world to finish the quest.",
	"quest-carp-beams": "Support Beams",
	"quest-carp-beams-desc": "Support beams hold up roofs and mine tunnels.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Craft support beams from logs or boards.",
	"quest-carp-table": "Build a Table",
	"quest-carp-table-desc": "A table makes a house a home.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Craft a table from boards. Set it down in the world to finish the quest.",
	"quest-carp-chair": "Build a Chair",
	"quest-carp-chair-desc": "Your settlers like to sit down to eat.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Craft a chair from boards. Set it down in the world to finish the quest.",
	"quest-carp-bed": "Build a Wooden Bed",
	"quest-carp-bed-desc": "A wooden bed lets you sleep longer than a bed of hay.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Craft a wooden bed from boards and cloth or hay. Set it down in the world to finish the quest.",
	"quest-carp-sign": "Make a Sign",
	"quest-carp-sign-desc": "Signs label chests and mark the way.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Craft a sign from boards. Writing on it needs a pigment such as charcoal. Set it down in the world to finish the quest.",
	"quest-carp-toolrack": "Build a Tool Rack",
	"quest-carp-toolrack-desc": "A tool rack hangs four tools on the wall.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Craft a tool rack from boards and sticks. Set it down in the world to finish the quest.",
	"objective-line-carp-bookshelf-0": "Place a bookshelf",
	"quest-carp-bookshelf": "Build a Bookshelf",
	"quest-carp-bookshelf-desc": "Bookshelves hold books and scrolls.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Craft a bookshelf from boards. Set it down in the world to finish the quest.",
	"quest-carp-axle": "Make a Wooden Axle",
	"quest-carp-axle-desc": "Axles carry the turning power of windmills and water wheels.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Craft a wooden axle from logs or boards. Set it down in the world to finish the quest.",
	"quest-carp-raft": "Build a Raft",
	"quest-carp-raft-desc": "A raft crosses water faster than swimming.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Craft a raft from logs and rope.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://gamemechanicinfo-shipbuilding\">ship building guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-carp-master": "Master Carpenter",
	"quest-carp-master-desc": "You have planted, felled, sawn and built.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Finish the quests that lead here, then claim it.",
	"quest-carp-brack": "Build a Barrel Rack",
	"quest-carp-brack-desc": "A barrel rack stores a barrel on its side with a tap.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Craft a barrel rack. The handbook shows the exact recipe. Set it down in the world to finish the quest.<br><br>Part of the Food Shelves mod.",
	"quest-carp-tun": "Make a Tun",
	"quest-carp-tun-desc": "A tun is a huge cask for liquids.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Craft a tun. The handbook shows the exact recipe. Set it down in the world to finish the quest.<br><br>Part of the Food Shelves mod.",
	"quest-carp-tunrack": "Build a Tun Rack",
	"quest-carp-tunrack-desc": "A tun rack holds a tun off the ground.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Craft a tun rack. The handbook shows the exact recipe. Set it down in the world to finish the quest.<br><br>Part of the Food Shelves mod.",
	"objective-line-carp-crate-0": "Place a wooden crate",
	"quest-carp-crate": "Build a Wooden Crate",
	"quest-carp-crate-desc": "A crate holds a great many of one kind of item.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Craft a wooden crate from boards and nails. Set it down in the world to finish the quest.",
	"chapter-carpentry": "Carpentry",
	"objective-line-herd-trap-0": "Have a basket trap",
	"quest-herd-trap": "Make a Basket Trap",
	"quest-herd-trap-desc": "A basket trap catches small animals alive.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Weave a basket trap from cattails or reeds in the crafting grid.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://gamemechanicinfo-animalhusbandry\">animal husbandry guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-herd-bait-0": "Place a trap",
	"quest-herd-bait": "Bait the Trap",
	"quest-herd-bait-desc": "Animals only walk into a baited trap.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Place the trap where small animals pass and right-click it with food they like. Stand close to it so the quest can see it.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://gamemechanicinfo-animalhusbandry\">animal husbandry guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-herd-catch-0": "A hare, chicken, raccoon or fox near you",
	"quest-herd-catch": "Catch a Small Animal",
	"quest-herd-catch-desc": "A caught animal can be carried home.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Check your trap now and then. When it has closed, pick it up with the animal inside and let the animal out in your pen. Stand near the animals so the quest can count them.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://gamemechanicinfo-animalhusbandry\">animal husbandry guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-herd-pen": "Build a Pen",
	"quest-herd-pen-desc": "A pen stops your animals from wandering off.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Build a ring of at least twelve fences with a gate. Stand beside it.<br><br><strong>Tip:</strong> Fences two high stop animals that jump.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://gamemechanicinfo-animalhusbandry\">animal husbandry guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-herd-first-1": "2 × farm animals near you",
	"quest-herd-first": "Pen Your First Animals",
	"quest-herd-first-desc": "Animals kept in a pen can be fed and bred.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Get two animals of one kind into your pen and close the gate. Stand near the animals so the quest can count them.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://gamemechanicinfo-animalhusbandry\">animal husbandry guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-herd-strough-0": "Place a small trough",
	"quest-herd-strough": "Make a Small Trough",
	"quest-herd-strough-desc": "Animals eat from a trough, not from your hand.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Craft a small trough from boards. Set it down in the world to finish the quest.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://gamemechanicinfo-animalhusbandry\">animal husbandry guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-herd-feed-0": "Look at a trough with feed in it",
	"quest-herd-feed": "Fill the Trough",
	"quest-herd-feed-desc": "Fed animals breed. Hungry ones do not.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Right-click the trough with grain, dry grass, vegetables or fruit. Look at the trough with feed in it.<br><br><strong>Tip:</strong> Different animals eat different feed. The handbook lists which.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://gamemechanicinfo-animalhusbandry\">animal husbandry guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-herd-ltrough-0": "Place a large trough",
	"quest-herd-ltrough": "Make a Large Trough",
	"quest-herd-ltrough-desc": "The large trough feeds pigs, sheep and other big animals.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Craft a large trough from boards. Set it down in the world to finish the quest.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://gamemechanicinfo-animalhusbandry\">animal husbandry guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-herd-keep-0": "A trough near you",
	"objective-line-herd-keep-1": "2 × farm animals near you",
	"quest-herd-keep": "Keep Livestock",
	"quest-herd-keep-desc": "A herd gives meat, hides, milk, eggs and wool without the hunt.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Finish the quests that lead here. Then stand by a trough with two of your animals near you.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://gamemechanicinfo-animalhusbandry\">animal husbandry guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-herd-hares-0": "2 × hares near you",
	"quest-herd-hares": "Keep Hares",
	"quest-herd-hares-desc": "Hares breed fast and need little room.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Keep two hares in a pen. Stand near the animals so the quest can count them.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://gamemechanicinfo-animalhusbandry\">animal husbandry guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-herd-goats-0": "2 × goats near you",
	"quest-herd-goats": "Keep Goats",
	"quest-herd-goats-desc": "Goats give milk and meat.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Keep two goats in a pen. Stand near the animals so the quest can count them.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://gamemechanicinfo-animalhusbandry\">animal husbandry guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-herd-chickens-0": "2 × chickens near you",
	"quest-herd-chickens": "Keep Chickens",
	"quest-herd-chickens-desc": "Chickens give eggs and feathers.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Keep two chickens in a pen. Stand near the animals so the quest can count them.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://gamemechanicinfo-animalhusbandry\">animal husbandry guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-herd-sheep-0": "2 × sheep near you",
	"quest-herd-sheep": "Keep Sheep",
	"quest-herd-sheep-desc": "Sheep give milk, meat and hides.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Keep two sheep in a pen. Stand near the animals so the quest can count them.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://gamemechanicinfo-animalhusbandry\">animal husbandry guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-herd-pigs-0": "2 × pigs near you",
	"quest-herd-pigs": "Keep Pigs",
	"quest-herd-pigs-desc": "Pigs give the most meat and fat.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Keep two pigs in a pen. Stand near the animals so the quest can count them.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://gamemechanicinfo-animalhusbandry\">animal husbandry guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-herd-henbox-0": "Place a henbox",
	"quest-herd-henbox": "Build a Henbox",
	"quest-herd-henbox-desc": "Hens lay their eggs in a henbox.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Craft a henbox from hay or dry grass. Set it down in the world to finish the quest.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://gamemechanicinfo-animalhusbandry\">animal husbandry guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-herd-eggs": "Collect Eggs",
	"quest-herd-eggs-desc": "Well fed hens lay eggs every few days.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Place a henbox in the chicken pen, keep the trough full, and collect the eggs.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://gamemechanicinfo-animalhusbandry\">animal husbandry guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-herd-chicks-0": "A chick near you",
	"quest-herd-chicks": "Hatch Chicks",
	"quest-herd-chicks-desc": "Eggs left in the henbox can hatch.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Keep a rooster with your hens and leave the eggs in the henbox. Stand near the animals so the quest can count them.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://gamemechanicinfo-animalhusbandry\">animal husbandry guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-herd-feathers": "Collect Feathers",
	"quest-herd-feathers-desc": "Feathers fletch arrows.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Chickens drop feathers when butchered.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://gamemechanicinfo-animalhusbandry\">animal husbandry guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-herd-breed-0": "An animal born in your pen near you",
	"quest-herd-breed": "Breed Your Animals",
	"quest-herd-breed-desc": "A male and a female that are well fed will have young.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Keep a pair in a pen with a full trough and wait. Stand near the animals so the quest can count them.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://gamemechanicinfo-animalhusbandry\">animal husbandry guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-herd-gen2-0": "A second generation animal near you",
	"quest-herd-gen2": "Raise a Second Generation",
	"quest-herd-gen2-desc": "Each generation born in your pen is calmer than the last.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Raise young that were born to animals in your pen. The quest wants an animal of the second generation. Stand near the animals so the quest can count them.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://gamemechanicinfo-animalhusbandry\">animal husbandry guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-herd-tame-0": "3 × third generation animals near you",
	"quest-herd-tame": "Raise a Tame Herd",
	"quest-herd-tame-desc": "After a few generations animals no longer run from you.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Keep breeding until you have three animals of the third generation. Stand near the animals so the quest can count them.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://gamemechanicinfo-animalhusbandry\">animal husbandry guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-herd-milk": "Milk an Animal",
	"quest-herd-milk-desc": "Tame mothers can be milked once a day.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Right-click a ewe or nanny goat that has had young with an empty bucket. Carry it in a bucket, bowl or jug, or look at the barrel or pot that holds it.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://gamemechanicinfo-animalhusbandry\">animal husbandry guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-herd-butcher-0": "Have any raw meat",
	"quest-herd-butcher": "Butcher an Animal",
	"quest-herd-butcher-desc": "A carcass gives meat, hide, fat and bones.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Kill an animal, then hold right-click on the body with a knife. Carry raw meat and a raw hide.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://gamemechanicinfo-animalhusbandry\">animal husbandry guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-herd-hides": "Save the Hides",
	"quest-herd-hides-desc": "Raw hides rot, so use or cure them soon.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Carry a raw hide.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://gamemechanicinfo-animalhusbandry\">animal husbandry guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-herd-fat": "Collect Fat",
	"quest-herd-fat-desc": "Fat seals crocks, oils hides and makes candles.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Butcher an animal. Larger and well fed animals give more fat.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://gamemechanicinfo-animalhusbandry\">animal husbandry guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-herd-ride": "Saddle and Ride",
	"quest-herd-ride-desc": "A tamed elk carries you faster than you can walk.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Put a bridle and saddle on a tamed elk and get on.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://gamemechanicinfo-mountableanimals\">mountable animals guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-herd-master": "Master Herder",
	"quest-herd-master-desc": "You have trapped, penned, bred and ridden.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Finish the quests that lead here, then claim it.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://gamemechanicinfo-animalhusbandry\">animal husbandry guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-herd-calf": "Capture an Elk Calf",
	"quest-herd-calf-desc": "An elk has to be raised from a calf to be ridden.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Find wild elk and bring a calf home. Stand beside the calf. Stand near the animals so the quest can count them.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://gamemechanicinfo-mountableanimals\">mountable animals guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-herd-raise-0": "An elk near you",
	"quest-herd-raise": "Raise the Calf",
	"quest-herd-raise-desc": "A calf takes time and feed to grow.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Keep the calf in a pen with a full trough until it grows up. Stand near the animals so the quest can count them.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://gamemechanicinfo-mountableanimals\">mountable animals guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-herd-break-0": "A tamed elk near you",
	"quest-herd-break": "Saddle Break the Elk",
	"quest-herd-break-desc": "A grown elk must get used to the saddle.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Follow the handbook's steps to break in your elk. Stand near the animals so the quest can count them.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://gamemechanicinfo-mountableanimals\">mountable animals guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-herd-buy-0": "A tamed elk near you",
	"quest-herd-buy": "Buy an Elk from a Trader",
	"quest-herd-buy-desc": "Some traders sell elk that are already tame.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Buy an elk from a trader. Stand near the animals so the quest can count them.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://gamemechanicinfo-mountableanimals\">mountable animals guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-herd-pack-0": "Have saddlebags",
	"quest-herd-pack": "Pack Your Elk",
	"quest-herd-pack-desc": "Saddlebags let your elk carry cargo.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Craft saddlebags and put them on your elk. Carry a set for the quest.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://gamemechanicinfo-mountableanimals\">mountable animals guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-herd-ctrap": "Make a Crate Trap",
	"quest-herd-ctrap-desc": "A crate trap catches larger animals alive.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Craft a crate trap from boards.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://gamemechanicinfo-animalhusbandry\">animal husbandry guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-herd-big-0": "A pig, sheep, goat or deer near you",
	"quest-herd-big": "Catch a Large Animal",
	"quest-herd-big-desc": "Large animals are the start of a real herd.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Bait a crate trap for pigs, sheep or goats and bring the animal home. Stand near the animals so the quest can count them.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://gamemechanicinfo-animalhusbandry\">animal husbandry guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"chapter-husbandry": "Animal Husbandry",
	"quest-tailor-hides": "Collect Hides",
	"quest-tailor-hides-desc": "Every hide starts as a raw hide from a butchered animal.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Butcher an animal with a knife and carry a raw hide.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-leathermaking\">leather making guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-tailor-salt": "Salt a Hide",
	"quest-tailor-salt-desc": "Salt stops a hide from rotting until you have time to tan it.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Combine a raw hide with salt.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-leathermaking\">leather making guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-tailor-soak": "Soak a Hide",
	"quest-tailor-soak-desc": "Soaking loosens the hair.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Seal raw hides in a barrel of limewater or diluted borax and wait.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-leathermaking\">leather making guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-tailor-oil": "Oil a Hide",
	"quest-tailor-oil-desc": "An oiled hide becomes a pelt with the fur left on.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Combine a raw hide with fat in the crafting grid.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-leathermaking\">leather making guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-tailor-pelt": "Cure a Pelt",
	"quest-tailor-pelt-desc": "Pelts are the material for fur clothes.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Leave an oiled hide to cure. It turns into a pelt by itself.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-leathermaking\">leather making guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-tailor-fur-0": "Have any fur clothing or hide armour",
	"quest-tailor-fur": "Make Some Fur Clothes",
	"quest-tailor-fur-desc": "Fur keeps you warm through winter.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Craft any piece of fur clothing or hide armour from pelts.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-leathermaking\">leather making guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-tailor-scrape": "Scrape a Hide",
	"quest-tailor-scrape-desc": "The hair must come off before tanning.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Put a soaked hide in the crafting grid with a knife.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-leathermaking\">leather making guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-tailor-lime": "Make Limewater",
	"quest-tailor-lime-desc": "Limewater is the bath for soaking hides.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Mix lime with water in a barrel. Carry it in a bucket, bowl or jug, or look at the barrel or pot that holds it.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-leathermaking\">leather making guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-tailor-weak": "Make Weak Tannin",
	"quest-tailor-weak-desc": "Tannin is what turns hide into leather.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Seal oak or acacia logs with water in a barrel to make weak tannin. Carry it in a bucket, bowl or jug, or look at the barrel or pot that holds it.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-leathermaking\">leather making guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-tailor-strong": "Make Strong Tannin",
	"quest-tailor-strong-desc": "Strong tannin finishes the job.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Seal more oak or acacia logs in a barrel of weak tannin. Carry it in a bucket, bowl or jug, or look at the barrel or pot that holds it.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-leathermaking\">leather making guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-tailor-prep": "Prepare a Hide",
	"quest-tailor-prep-desc": "A prepared hide is ready for its last bath.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Seal scraped hides in a barrel of weak tannin and wait.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-leathermaking\">leather making guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-tailor-leather": "Make Leather",
	"quest-tailor-leather-desc": "Leather makes bags, armour, saddles and bellows.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Seal prepared hides in a barrel of strong tannin and wait.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-leathermaking\">leather making guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-tailor-backpack": "Make a Backpack",
	"quest-tailor-backpack-desc": "A backpack adds more slots than any basket.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Craft a leather backpack from leather.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-leathermaking\">leather making guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-tailor-findlime-0": "Have lime or powdered borax",
	"quest-tailor-findlime": "Find Lime or Borax",
	"quest-tailor-findlime-desc": "Lime and borax both soak hides.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Burn limestone or chalk to get lime, or find borax in dry lands.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-leathermaking\">leather making guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-tailor-saddle-0": "Have a saddle",
	"quest-tailor-saddle": "Make a Saddle",
	"quest-tailor-saddle-desc": "A saddle lets you ride.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Craft a saddle from leather.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-leathermaking\">leather making guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-tailor-bridle-0": "Have a bridle",
	"quest-tailor-bridle": "Make a Bridle",
	"quest-tailor-bridle-desc": "A bridle lets you steer your mount.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Craft a bridle from leather and a metal bit.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-leathermaking\">leather making guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-tailor-sleather": "Make Sturdy Leather",
	"quest-tailor-sleather-desc": "Sturdy leather is thicker and made from the largest hides.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Tan a huge hide the full way through to get sturdy leather.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-leathermaking\">leather making guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-tailor-sbackpack": "Make a Sturdy Backpack",
	"quest-tailor-sbackpack-desc": "The sturdy backpack is the largest bag you can wear.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Craft a sturdy backpack from sturdy leather.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-leathermaking\">leather making guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-tailor-armour-0": "Have a piece of leather armour",
	"quest-tailor-armour": "Make Leather Armour",
	"quest-tailor-armour-desc": "Leather armour is light and easy to move in.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Craft any piece of leather armour.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-leathermaking\">leather making guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-tailor-huge-0": "Have a huge hide that is soaked, scraped or prepared",
	"quest-tailor-huge": "Tan a Huge Hide",
	"quest-tailor-huge-desc": "Huge hides come from bears and other great beasts.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Take a huge hide through soaking, scraping and tanning.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-leathermaking\">leather making guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-tailor-master": "Master Tailor",
	"quest-tailor-master-desc": "You have tanned, woven, sewn and dyed.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Finish the quests that lead here, then claim it.",
	"quest-tailor-twine": "Make Twine",
	"quest-tailor-twine-desc": "Twine is spun from flax fibres.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Harvest flax for fibres and craft them into flax twine.",
	"quest-tailor-linen": "Weave Linen",
	"quest-tailor-linen-desc": "Linen is woven from twine.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Craft linen from flax twine in the crafting grid.",
	"quest-tailor-kit": "Make a Sewing Kit",
	"quest-tailor-kit-desc": "A sewing kit is needed to sew and mend clothes.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Craft a sewing kit.",
	"quest-tailor-sack": "Make a Linen Sack",
	"quest-tailor-sack-desc": "A linen sack is a bag made without any leather.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Craft a linen sack from linen and twine.",
	"quest-tailor-cloth": "Make Cloth",
	"quest-tailor-cloth-desc": "Cloth is the material for clothes.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Craft plain cloth from linen.",
	"quest-tailor-shirt": "Sew a Shirt",
	"quest-tailor-shirt-desc": "Clothes keep you warm, and good clothes last.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Sew any shirt or other upper body clothing.",
	"quest-tailor-trousers": "Sew Some Trousers",
	"quest-tailor-trousers-desc": "Warm legs matter as much as a warm chest.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Sew any trousers or other lower body clothing.",
	"objective-line-tailor-alum-0": "A mordant bath in a container you carry or look at",
	"quest-tailor-alum": "Prepare for Mordanted Cloth",
	"quest-tailor-alum-desc": "A mordant makes dye hold fast to cloth.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Dissolve alum, borax or another mordant in water in a barrel. Carry it in a bucket, bowl or jug, or look at the barrel or pot that holds it.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-dyemaking\">dye making guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-tailor-mordant": "Treat Cloth with Mordant",
	"quest-tailor-mordant-desc": "Cloth treated with mordant takes dye well.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Soak plain cloth in the mordant bath.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-dyemaking\">dye making guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-tailor-yellow": "Make Yellow Dye",
	"quest-tailor-yellow-desc": "Yellow is the easiest dye.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Make yellow dye from dye plants in a barrel of water. Carry it in a bucket, bowl or jug, or look at the barrel or pot that holds it.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-dyemaking\">dye making guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-tailor-dyecloth": "Dye Cloth Yellow",
	"quest-tailor-dyecloth-desc": "Dyed cloth makes coloured clothes and banners.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Soak mordanted cloth in yellow dye.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-dyemaking\">dye making guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"objective-line-tailor-woad-0": "Blue dye in a container you carry or look at",
	"quest-tailor-woad": "Make Woad Dye",
	"quest-tailor-woad-desc": "Blue dye comes from the woad plant.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Make woad dye from woad in a barrel. Carry it in a bucket, bowl or jug, or look at the barrel or pot that holds it.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-dyemaking\">dye making guide</a> in the handbook.",
	"quest-tailor-dyeblue": "Dye Cloth Blue",
	"quest-tailor-dyeblue-desc": "Blue cloth is the mark of a rich colony.<br><br><strong>How:</strong> Soak mordanted cloth in blue dye.<br><br>See the <a href=\"handbook://craftinginfo-dyemaking\">dye making guide</a> in the handbook.",
