	"workstatus-hunter-lost": "an animal got away",
	"activity-hunter-hunt": "Hunting",
	"activity-hunter-skin": "Skinning",
	"hunter-progress": "Animals killed: {0}.",
	"skill-hunting": "Hunting",
	"collect-hint-hunter": "The animals the hunter may hunt. Turn one off to leave it alone.",
	"job-butcher": "Butcher",
	"block-hut-butcher": "Butcher's Hut",
	"building-butcher": "Butcher's Hut",
	"hut-placed-butcher": "{0} placed. Give a settler the Butcher job and put a knife in the hut storage (sneak + right-click). Hunters bring their kills here.",
	"hint-butcher": "The butcher cuts up dead animals with a knife. It gets more meat and fat than skinning, plus bones. It picks up dead animals up to {0} blocks away.",
	"guide-butcher": "<strong>Butcher's Hut</strong><br>The butcher cuts up animals for meat, hides, fat and bones.<br><br><strong>Main</strong>: rename the hut, choose who works here, and order upgrades.<br><strong>Work area</strong>: how far out the butcher goes for dead animals.<br><br>Give it a knife. While you have a butcher, the hunter brings its kills here whole instead of skinning them. The butcher also picks up dead animals on your land, and ones left at the Hunter's Hut or in the warehouse.<br><br>It gets a quarter more meat and fat than skinning, plus bones. Couriers take it all to the warehouse, food to the coolest chests or cellar first.<br><br>With the Butchering mod, put a hook or table in the hut for a bit more meat. Put empty buckets in the hut storage and the butcher fills them with blood.",
	"workarea-range-hint-butcher": "The butcher picks up dead animals in this range.",
