	"hut-placed-mint": "{0} placed. Right-click it to order level 1, give a settler the Minter job, and put a hammer in its storage (sneak + right-click). Couriers bring ingots of the coin's metal.",
	"hint-mint": "The minter strikes copies of the colony's Coinage coin from ingots of its metal, with a hammer. The coins are the colony's treasury. The bailiff pays wages from it.",
	"guide-mint": "<strong>Royal Mint</strong><br>Needs the Coinage mod. The minter strikes the colony's Coinage coins.<br><br><strong>Main</strong>: rename the hut, choose who works here, and order upgrades.<br><br>The minter needs a hammer and ingots of the coin's metal. One ingot makes 10 coins, and the minter keeps 100 struck. Coins in the Mint, the Town Hall's chests and the warehouse are the treasury. On the first day of each month the bailiff collects taxes into it and pays wages out of it (Town Hall, Bailiff tab).<br><br>Design a coin with Coinage, hold it and press <strong>Use the coin in my hand</strong> on the Bailiff tab's Taxes & wages page. Until then any Coinage coin counts.<br><br>Without Coinage the colony pays in rusty gears and has no Mint.",
