	"couriers-empty": "Carrying nothing",
	"guide-courierstation": "<strong>Courier's Station</strong><br>A work station for the Warehouse. Put it inside the Warehouse building, or near the Warehouse block.<br><br><strong>Couriers</strong>: how many couriers there are, what each is doing, where they take things from and to, and what they carry. Settlers without a job show up while they help.<br><br>To get more couriers, give settlers the Courier job in the Town Hall.",
	"block-hut-archive": "Archive",
	"building-archive": "Archive",
	"job-researcher": "Researcher",
	"skill-research": "Research",
	"hut-placed-archive": "{0} placed. Right-click it to order level 1 and give settlers the Researcher job. Start research on its Research tab.",
	"archive-needs-townhall": "The Archive needs a level 2 Town Hall.",
	"hint-archive": "Researchers study here. Pick what to research on the Research tab. A table, a shelf with books and a light nearby make them faster. Forges and saws close by slow them down. Put a chair or stool beside a table and they sit there to write. Hand in books, relics and field notes on the Research tab.",
	"guide-archive": "<strong>Archive</strong><br>Researchers study the colony's research tree here.<br><br><strong>Main</strong>: rename the hut, choose who works here, and order upgrades.<br><strong>Research</strong>: start, pause and follow research.<br><br>Each tier runs one more research at once and takes two more researchers. Research costs items, which couriers bring here, and Research Points, which researchers make by studying.<br><br>Research is faster with a table, a shelf with books and a light near the hut block. Smelters, forges, saws and quarries nearby slow it down.<br><br>Tier 3 research needs an Archive at tier 2, and tier 4 an Archive at tier 3.<br><br><strong>Hand in</strong>: hold a book, a lore journal, a resonance archive, a ruin find, field notes or a temporal gear and press Hand in. They give Research Points (up to 300 a day) or Knowledge Tokens. Points go to the oldest research running here, or are stored for the next one. Rusty gears are money, so the Archive does not take them.<br><br><strong>Field trips</strong>: once Field Notes is done, Explorers visit ruins, translocators and peaks the Archive offers, write Field notes and bring them here. Keep parchment in the Explorer's Hut.<br><br>Now and then an experiment fails and a few hours of work are lost. Skilled researchers in a good room fail less. Sometimes they make a lucky find instead.<br><br>Finished research helps the whole colony and is kept even if the Archive is removed.",
	"archive-info": "Research: {0} of {1} running, {2} done, {3} Knowledge Tokens",
