	"job-chickenherder": "Chicken Herder",
	"block-hut-chickencoop": "Chicken Coop",
	"building-chickencoop": "Chicken Coop",
	"hut-placed-chickencoop": "{0} placed. Give a settler the Chicken Herder job. It looks after the chickens near the hut.",
	"hint-chickencoop": "The pen is everything up to {0} blocks from the hut. The chicken herder fills the troughs there with feed. It collects the eggs from nest boxes. When there are too many hens, it culls the spare grown ones with a knife.",
	"guide-chickencoop": "<strong>Chicken Coop</strong><br>The chicken herder looks after the chickens in a pen by the hut.<br><br><strong>Main</strong>: rename the hut, choose who works here, and order upgrades.<br><strong>Work area</strong>: how far the pen reaches.<br><br>Build a fence around the hut, put troughs and nest boxes feed inside, and lead two or more chickens in. The chicken herder needs a knife. It fills the troughs from the hut's storage, or asks couriers to bring feed from the warehouse. Fed animals breed.<br><br>Each level keeps more animals. Above that, it culls the spare grown ones, but always keeps a male and two females. It skins them and brings the meat and hides here. Couriers take them to the warehouse. Named and tamed animals are never culled.",
	"workarea-range-hint-chickencoop": "The pen reaches this far.",
	"job-swineherd": "Swineherd",
	"block-hut-piggery": "Piggery",
	"building-piggery": "Piggery",
	"hut-placed-piggery": "{0} placed. Give a settler the Swineherd job. It looks after the pigs near the hut.",
	"hint-piggery": "The pen is everything up to {0} blocks from the hut. The swineherd fills the troughs there with feed. When there are too many pigs, it culls the spare grown ones with a knife.",
	"guide-piggery": "<strong>Piggery</strong><br>The swineherd looks after the pigs in a pen by the hut.<br><br><strong>Main</strong>: rename the hut, choose who works here, and order upgrades.<br><strong>Work area</strong>: how far the pen reaches.<br><br>Build a fence around the hut, put troughs and feed inside, and lead two or more pigs in. The swineherd needs a knife. It fills the troughs from the hut's storage, or asks couriers to bring feed from the warehouse. Fed animals breed.<br><br>Each level keeps more animals. Above that, it culls the spare grown ones, but always keeps a male and two females. It skins them and brings the meat and hides here. Couriers take them to the warehouse. Named and tamed animals are never culled.",
	"workarea-range-hint-piggery": "The pen reaches this far.",
	"job-shepherd": "Shepherd",
	"block-hut-shepherd": "Shepherd's Hut",
	"building-shepherd": "Shepherd's Hut",
	"hut-placed-shepherd": "{0} placed. Give a settler the Shepherd job. It looks after the sheep near the hut.",
	"hint-shepherd": "The pen is everything up to {0} blocks from the hut. The shepherd fills the troughs there with feed. It milks them into empty buckets. When there are too many sheep, it culls the spare grown ones with a knife.",
	"guide-shepherd": "<strong>Shepherd's Hut</strong><br>The shepherd looks after the sheep in a pen by the hut.<br><br><strong>Main</strong>: rename the hut, choose who works here, and order upgrades.<br><strong>Work area</strong>: how far the pen reaches.<br><br>Build a fence around the hut, put troughs and feed inside, and lead two or more sheep in. The shepherd needs a knife. It fills the troughs from the hut's storage, or asks couriers to bring feed from the warehouse. Fed animals breed.<br><br>Each level keeps more animals. Above that, it culls the spare grown ones, but always keeps a male and two females. It skins them and brings the meat and hides here. Couriers take them to the warehouse. Named and tamed animals are never culled.",
	"workarea-range-hint-shepherd": "The pen reaches this far.",
	"job-goatherd": "Goatherd",
	"block-hut-goatherd": "Goatherd's Hut",
	"building-goatherd": "Goatherd's Hut",
	"hut-placed-goatherd": "{0} placed. Give a settler the Goatherd job. It looks after the goats near the hut.",
	"hint-goatherd": "The pen is everything up to {0} blocks from the hut. The goatherd fills the troughs there with feed. It milks them into empty buckets. When there are too many goats, it culls the spare grown ones with a knife.",
	"guide-goatherd": "<strong>Goatherd's Hut</strong><br>The goatherd looks after the goats in a pen by the hut.<br><br><strong>Main</strong>: rename the hut, choose who works here, and order upgrades.<br><strong>Work area</strong>: how far the pen reaches.<br><br>Build a fence around the hut, put troughs and feed inside, and lead two or more goats in. The goatherd needs a knife. It fills the troughs from the hut's storage, or asks couriers to bring feed from the warehouse. Fed animals breed.<br><br>Each level keeps more animals. Above that, it culls the spare grown ones, but always keeps a male and two females. It skins them and brings the meat and hides here. Couriers take them to the warehouse. Named and tamed animals are never culled.",
	"workarea-range-hint-goatherd": "The pen reaches this far.",
	"job-herdsman": "Herdsman",
	"block-hut-herdsman": "Herdsman's Hut",
	"building-herdsman": "Herdsman's Hut",
	"hut-placed-herdsman": "{0} placed. Give a settler the Herdsman job. It looks after the farm animals near the hut.",
	"hint-herdsman": "The pen is everything up to {0} blocks from the hut. The herdsman fills the troughs there with feed. It collects the eggs from nest boxes. It milks them into empty buckets. When there are too many animals, it culls the spare grown ones with a knife. It looks after any animal that breeds, from other mods too.",
	"guide-herdsman": "<strong>Herdsman's Hut</strong><br>The herdsman looks after the farm animals in a pen by the hut.<br><br><strong>Main</strong>: rename the hut, choose who works here, and order upgrades.<br><strong>Work area</strong>: how far the pen reaches.<br><br>Build a fence around the hut, put troughs and nest boxes feed inside, and lead two or more farm animals in. The herdsman needs a knife. It fills the troughs from the hut's storage, or asks couriers to bring feed from the warehouse. Fed animals breed.<br><br>Each level keeps more animals. Above that, it culls the spare grown ones, but always keeps a male and two females. It skins them and brings the meat and hides here. Couriers take them to the warehouse. Named and tamed animals are never culled.",
	"workarea-range-hint-herdsman": "The pen reaches this far.",
