	"block-hut-tannery": "Tannery",
	"building-tannery": "Tannery",
	"hut-placed-tannery": "{0} placed. Give a settler the Tanner job. The tanner makes leather from hides in barrels near the hut.",
	"hint-tannery": "The tanner uses the barrels near the hut. It makes limewater, soaks the hides, scrapes them, then tans them into leather.",
	"guide-tannery": "<strong>Tannery</strong><br>The tanner makes leather from raw hides, the game's way.<br><br><strong>Main</strong>: rename the hut, choose who works here, and order upgrades.<br><br>Put a few barrels next to the hut. The tanner needs a knife and a bucket. It fetches water and makes limewater with lime (or borax water with borax). It soaks the hides, scrapes them with the knife, then soaks them in weak tannin and strong tannin made from oak or acacia logs. It asks couriers for hides, lime and logs from the warehouse. The leather goes to the warehouse.<br><br>Tanning takes days. Each barrel holds one step at a time, so more barrels make more leather.",
