	"hint-market": "The Market Trader brings meals and good clothes from the warehouse to the stall. Settlers with spare money buy them. What they pay goes to the treasury.",
	"guide-market": "<strong>Market</strong><br>Settlers spend their money here.<br><br><strong>Main</strong>: rename the hut, choose who works here, and order upgrades.<br><strong>For sale</strong>: what is sold, how many are on the stall, and the price. Officers change prices and turn things on or off.<br><br>The Market Trader brings cooked meals and clothes in good condition from the warehouse. It never takes more than half of what the warehouse has, so settlers with no money still eat and dress for free. Settlers keep 5 gears and spend the rest. Hungry settlers who can pay buy a meal here. Settlers whose clothes are worn buy new ones and leave the old ones for the Tailor. Everything they pay goes to the treasury.<br><br>Starts when the Town Hall is level 2.",
